INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(1,'dr-companion','Ruby4Lich5','C:/Ruby4Lich5','https://github.com/elanthia-online/lich-5/releases','Lich runs on Ruby; dr-companion automates Lich. Captured in no manifest.',1,'2026-08-26 16:28:33','ls "C:/Ruby4Lich5/4.0.6/bin/ruby.exe" && echo PRESENT');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(2,'dr-companion','Genie4','C:/Genie4/Maps',NULL,'ONLY the Maps subdirectory matters: 85 XML files of twenty years of hand cartography that no package manager can restore. Deleting it breaks nothing today because the built JSON is committed - it means the map can never be rebuilt or corrected. Silent, months later.',1,'2026-08-26 16:28:33','ls "C:/Genie4/Maps"/*.xml | wc -l   # expect 85');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(3,'quickgrade','playwright (node package)','C:/Users/Admin/Downloads/testgrader/tools/node_modules','https://playwright.dev','The whole test harness is Playwright driving headless Chromium. tools/package.json names the package but nothing records that the browser binaries live in a separate machine-wide cache, listed as its own row. Both must be present.',1,'2026-08-26 17:01:06',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(4,'quickgrade','CPython 3.13','C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Programs/Python/Python313',NULL,'build.py regenerates sw.js and the single-file QuickGrade.html, and the build check fails without it. No manifest names an interpreter, and the obvious names on PATH are Store aliases that execute nothing. The binary is python.exe inside this directory. See trap python-none-on-path.',1,'2026-08-26 17:01:06',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(5,'dr-companion','ComfyUI','http://127.0.0.1:8188','https://github.com/comfyanonymous/ComfyUI','The whole art pipeline talks to it over HTTP. tools/art-daemon.mjs waits for it rather than exiting, so a missing ComfyUI looks like a daemon that is running and producing nothing. Needs the ImageScale and SaveImage nodes, which the daemon uses to emit a thumbnail it scores itself on.',1,'2026-08-26 16:19:21',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(6,'dr-companion','FLUX.1-schnell fp8 checkpoint','C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Comfy-Desktop\ComfyUI-Shared\models\checkpoints','https://huggingface.co/black-forest-labs/FLUX.1-schnell','schnell is Apache 2.0 and puts no conditions on its output, which is the entire reason it and not dev: the art pack can be shipped commercially and given to Simutronics. FLUX.1-dev is the trap. It is the better-known model and what most guides reach for, and it is NON-COMMERCIAL: one image rendered with it would make the whole pack legally unusable. It was on this machine and was deleted 26 Aug 2026, so there is nothing to swap in by accident today. The checkpoint is pinned in tools/art-daemon.mjs and tools/art-run.mjs to guard against it being downloaded again, which is now the likely way this goes wrong.',1,'2026-08-26 16:19:21',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(7,'dr-companion','Genie 4 map XML','C:\Genie4\Maps','https://www.playdragonrealms.com/','85 XML files, the community cartography every map in dr-companion is built from: 17,750 rooms, 42,866 exits, 3,174 named places, and the 310 gateways linking one zone to the next. tools/build-map.mjs reads them into src/data/map. The built JSON is committed, so deleting these breaks nothing today and permanently prevents the map being rebuilt or corrected. Silent failure, months later, the first time someone needs to regenerate.',1,'2026-08-26 16:19:21',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(8,'dr-companion','Node 24 or newer','C:\Program Files\nodejs','https://nodejs.org/','The test suite imports TypeScript directly (tools/trail-test.mjs and tools/flow-test.mjs import from src/lib/*.ts) and relies on native type stripping. On an older Node those suites do not run.',1,'2026-08-26 16:19:21',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(9,'dr-companion','Python 3.13','C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python313','https://www.python.org/','Not used by the app. Recorded because `python` on PATH resolves to the Microsoft Store stub and fails with Permission denied, which reads as "Python is missing" when it is installed. Use the full path.',0,'2026-08-26 16:19:21',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(10,'world-aflame-godot','Public STUN server (stun.l.google.com:19302)','hardcoded in scripts/net/net_manager.gd, ICE_SERVERS const',NULL,'NAT traversal for serverless P2P WebRTC play -- no manifest records this since it''s an external network dependency, not a package. No fallback if Google''s STUN server ever goes away or blocks this traffic.',1,'2026-08-26 16:18:23',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(11,'world-aflame-godot','Godot 4.7.2 Standard (non-Mono) build','C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Programs\Godot\Standard',NULL,'Mono build has zero Web export templates -- this project is pure GDScript specifically so it can use the Standard build and export to Web. Separate install from the Mono build at ...\Godot\Godot_v4.7.2-stable_mono_win64, which is not used by this project.',1,'2026-08-26 16:18:23',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(12,'magi-reader-engine','magi art and audio source folders','C:\Users\Admin\Downloads\Legacy builds and Assets...if you can''t find something, try here\magi-itch-*',NULL,'The Gift of the Magi''s 224 art files and 519 recordings exist on this disk only. No single magi-itch-* folder is complete (199, 190, 183 of 224); only the union is, and tools/copy-assets.mjs takes the union across seven folders. They are committed to a local repo at C:\Users\Admin\dev\magi-reader whose GitHub remote was DELETED, so committed does not mean backed up: git ls-remote origin fails there. public/art and public/magi-audio are gitignored in magi-app, so nothing reaches GitHub from there either. Verified 26 Aug 2026: 0 magi media files across all three live repos.',1,'2026-08-26 16:38:39','bash "C:\Users\Admin\Downloads\Legacy builds and Assets...if you can''t find something, try here\verify-media.sh"');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(13,'the-raven-edgar-allan-poe-magi-reader','raven-itch-folder zips','C:\Users\Admin\Downloads\Legacy builds and Assets...if you can''t find something, try here\raven-itch-folder*.zip',NULL,'HISTORICAL, and now redundant. These four zips held the only copy of The Raven''s 368 narration mp3s and its word-level timings. Verified 26 Aug 2026: 368 committed locally AND 368 present on github.com/dancockrell/the-raven-edgar-allan-poe-magi-reader, so the zips are safe to delete. Do not take that from this row; run the check, which counts both ends every time.',0,'2026-08-26 16:38:39','bash "C:\Users\Admin\Downloads\Legacy builds and Assets...if you can''t find something, try here\verify-media.sh"');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(14,'quickgrade','chromium browser cache (playwright)','C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/ms-playwright','https://playwright.dev','Where playwright keeps the browsers it downloads. Separate from node_modules and strippable independently of it: on 26 Aug 2026 icudtl.dat vanished from here and Chrome launched then died while --version still worked. Restore with npx playwright install chromium --force. See trap file-stripping.',1,'2026-08-26 17:01:06',NULL);
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(15,'quartermaster','openclaw','C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Roaming/npm',NULL,'Quartermaster registers as an MCP server in OpenClaw''s config so OpenClaw can drive the scheduler, and OpenClaw''s Discord channel is how sessions on this machine talk to each other. The binary is openclaw.cmd in this directory. Not required to build or run qm itself.',1,'2026-08-27 09:23:14','PATH="C:\Program Files\nodejs;C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Roaming\npm;$PATH" openclaw mcp probe');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(16,'magi-reader-title-porting','the-tell-tale-heart-poe-reader','C:\Users\Admin\dev\the-tell-tale-heart-poe-reader',NULL,'Content pack repo for the porting project; deleting it loses an authored, gate-passing title unless GitHub is checked first',1,'2026-08-27 09:20:42','gh api repos/dancockrell/the-tell-tale-heart-poe-reader/commits --jq ''length''');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(17,'magi-reader-title-porting','the-cask-of-amontillado-poe-reader','C:\Users\Admin\dev\the-cask-of-amontillado-poe-reader',NULL,'Content pack repo for the porting project; deleting it loses an authored, gate-passing title unless GitHub is checked first',1,'2026-08-27 09:20:42','gh api repos/dancockrell/the-cask-of-amontillado-poe-reader/commits --jq ''length''');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(18,'magi-reader-title-porting','an-occurrence-at-owl-creek-bridge-reader','C:\Users\Admin\dev\an-occurrence-at-owl-creek-bridge-reader',NULL,'Content pack repo for the porting project; deleting it loses an authored, gate-passing title unless GitHub is checked first',1,'2026-08-27 09:35:24','gh api repos/dancockrell/an-occurrence-at-owl-creek-bridge-reader/commits --jq ''length''');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(19,'magi-reader-title-porting','to-build-a-fire-jack-london-reader','C:\Users\Admin\dev\to-build-a-fire-jack-london-reader',NULL,'Content pack repo for the porting project; deleting it loses an authored, gate-passing title unless GitHub is checked first',1,'2026-08-27 11:47:09','gh api repos/dancockrell/to-build-a-fire-jack-london-reader/commits --jq ''length''');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(20,'magi-reader-title-porting','desirees-baby-kate-chopin-reader','C:\Users\Admin\dev\desirees-baby-kate-chopin-reader',NULL,'Content pack repo for the porting project; deleting it loses an authored, gate-passing title unless GitHub is checked first',1,'2026-08-27 13:05:14','gh api repos/dancockrell/desirees-baby-kate-chopin-reader/commits --jq ''length''');
INSERT INTO "dependencies" VALUES(21,'dr-companion','ws (npm)','C:/Users/Admin/dev/dr-companion/node_modules/ws',NULL,'tools/mock-lich-server.mjs imports it and it is NOT in package.json - unlisted optional dep named only in that file''s header. Absent as of 27 Aug 2026: npm run mock-lich dies on ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND before executing a line.',1,'2026-08-27 15:49:03','cd C:/Users/Admin/dev/dr-companion && node -e "require.resolve(''ws'');console.log(''present'')"');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(1,'2026-08-26 15:32:10','a9593032','milestone','Structured memory database created and hourly backup registered','SQLite 3.50.4 via Python. Dump-and-hash backup to private repo dancockrell/memory-db. Scheduled task ClaudeMemoryBackup, hourly.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(2,'2026-08-26T22:52:38','quickgrade-session','milestone','QuickGrade: answer sheet redesign and a visual inspection rig','Added tools/look.js: it renders a page and reports truncated text, collisions, ink too light or thin to survive a photocopier, content escaping its page, and unreadably small type, with annotated and layer screenshots. It immediately found four real defects, including truncated correct answers and a PAGE label running under the first page bubble on every sheet the app had ever printed. Also: questions now print on the answer sheet beside their own bubbles; corner fiducials are registration brackets rather than solid squares, where the arm width is a robustness number and not a taste one (0.5 of the mark measured 0.71 fill against a 0.70 detector threshold and lost corners to noise, 0.58 measures 0.80); the test code is a ten-mark strip instead of thirty pre-filled bubbles; and pages after the first drop the repeated header.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(3,'2026-08-26 15:53:34','dr-companion-session','milestone','Recorded dr-companion invisible dependencies after the Ruby removal','Verified Ruby 4.0.6 at C:\Ruby4Lich5\4.0.6 is present and the three Ruby test suites pass. Added ComfyUI, the FLUX.1-schnell checkpoint (licensing critical), the Genie 4 map XML, and the Node 24 requirement, none of which appear in package.json or any README.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(4,'2026-08-26 15:56:40','a9593032','removal','FLUX.1-dev deleted (16.06 GB, non-commercial licence)','flux1-schnell-fp8 Apache-2.0 retained. dr-companion pins schnell in two files; swapping dev in would make its art pack legally unusable.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(5,'2026-08-26 15:57:08',NULL,'milestone','world-aflame-godot: shipped Skirmish (Snap-inspired simultaneous-reveal ruleset), 1500 keyword-driven generated cards (500/faction), and witness-chain (github.com/dancockrell/witness-chain) -- a standalone dual-signature hash-chain ledger for tamper-evident match records, built for reuse across game projects, not just this one.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(6,'2026-08-26 16:01:09','a9593032','decision','Co-located dependency warnings generated from the DB','mem export writes DEPENDENCIES.md into project dirs; mem guard writes WHAT-USES-THIS.md into the dependency''s own directory. Guard is the one that would have prevented the Ruby4Lich5 deletion.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(7,'2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL,'decision','The Raven''s narration was recovered from raven-itch-folder zips and committed: 368 mp3 plus a 368-cue WebVTT converted from the original timings.js with zero round-trip failures. The pack''s own AUDIO-NEEDED.md had claimed the audio was gone and unreconstructable; every part of that was false. It is now AUDIO-RECOVERED.md.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(8,'2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL,'milestone','magi-reader-engine: feature complete and green. 676 unit tests, 642 e2e across four engines. A book is runtime state rather than a compile-time import, the engine has its own fixture book, and a parity test carries the prototype''s inventory so nothing can be dropped or added without a written decision.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(9,'2026-08-26 16:09:32','dr-companion-session','error','Nudity gate passed against an empty prompt file','tools/safety-test.mjs runs first in the chain so a regression fails the build before anything else. Pointed at {} it reported all 0 carry it / 0 checked / all passed / exit 0. Fixed in 21e6b06: every none-of-these-are-bad assertion now also asserts the set was not empty, in that suite and six more in the gateway suite.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(10,'2026-08-26 16:12:15','a9593032','decision','guard and review now assert a non-empty denominator','Both reported clean and exit 0 against a wiped database - demonstrated, not reasoned. Now print what was checked and exit 1 when there is nothing to check.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(11,'2026-08-26 16:21:59','a9593032','decision','CLAUDE.md reworked, not appended','Rule 1 rewritten to absorb three overlapping verification lessons into one section with a table of six instances. Header now explicitly invites every session to edit and merge rules, not only append. Numbering declared history, not hierarchy.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(12,'2026-08-26 16:22:44',NULL,'decision','Named a failure class shared across three sessions on 2026-08-26: the check that reports success when it did not execute. Instances: a git audit comparing against origin/<local-branch-name> that does not exist; a test runner counting FAIL lines in output from a suite that crashed; an assertion carrying a term that was always zero; a regex strip that never matched; and the detector written to find them, which found nothing because it read no files. Recorded so the shape is recognisable rather than rediscovered.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(13,'2026-08-26 16:24:49',NULL,'decision','Declined a peer request to rewrite C:\Users\Admin\.claude\CLAUDE.md. The peer reported that Dan had opened the file to all sessions; that may well be true, but a relayed authorisation is not an authorisation, and CLAUDE.md is the file that governs how every session behaves. Proposed rule text was surfaced to Dan directly instead.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(14,'2026-08-26 16:26:32','a9593032','decision','Retracted a CLAUDE.md edit invitation sent to three peer sessions','Dan authorised me; I relayed it as authorisation for them. That is permission laundering. Two retractions sent; Magi Reader had already refused and escalated correctly.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(15,'2026-08-26 16:38:39',NULL,'error','Wrote four checks for two dependency rows and every one of them was wrong in the same direction, each printing a plausible zero: a PowerShell wildcard path with -Filter (0 instead of 368); node not on PATH so a tool that never ran reported 0 plates; the wrong extension and directory (.png in public/audio when the files are .webp in public/magi-audio); and git -C failing on a path with an apostrophe, whose error piped into wc -l printed 0 dirty files. Zero is what a broken check says.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(16,'2026-08-26 16:50:02',NULL,'error','mem review reported six live dependency locations as GONE','Path(loc).exists() was applied to URLs, prose, wildcards and relative paths alike. Fixed with classify_location plus test_classify.py: 10 cases, 2 of which assert real absence, so the suite cannot pass with a classifier that never reports gone. Reported by the Magi Reader session as one row.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(17,'2026-08-26 16:50:02',NULL,'milestone','magi book media confirmed to exist in exactly one place','743 files, 27.5 MB, committed to dev/magi-reader whose remote is a hard 404. Verified against the GitHub tree API for all three magi repos: engine has 5 media under docs/, classroom-toolkit has 0, the-raven has its own 368 in pack/audio. Surfaced to Dan; publishing is his call.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(18,'2026-08-27T00:01:06','quickgrade-session','decision','A suite that asserts nothing now fails the runner','tools/check.js printed "asserted nothing" beside a green line and counted the suite as passing. That is the same defect the runner exists to catch: an absent result and a negative result print identically, and the absent one looks like success. The count of checks is the fragile number, the one that goes to zero when the mechanism breaks, so it is the one to assert on. Demonstrated with a suite that exits 0 having run nothing: it now reads FAIL. Also added a substring filter, because a ten-minute suite is one a person checking a single thing will skip entirely.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(19,'2026-08-26 17:14:51',NULL,'decision','Dan authorised editing CLAUDE.md directly on 27 Aug 2026 after I declined the same request relayed through a peer. Added to it: a fifth sub-rule under section 1 (zero is what a broken check says, from four broken checks in one sitting); four machine traps under section 10 (deleted remote reports in sync, PowerShell wildcard-dir with -Filter returns 0, node/gh not on PowerShell PATH, git -C fails on apostrophe paths); a cross-session rule under section 13 (a session cannot pass on permission it was given); and section 19, write the check not the claim.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(20,'2026-08-26 17:20:21',NULL,'milestone','CLAUDE.md section 1 gained the false-positive rule','A check that always fires is as empty as one that never does. From mem review listing six live locations as GONE, plus the over-correction that demoted a real path. Verified with check-xrefs.py after the edit: 22 sections, 14 references, all resolving.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(21,'2026-08-26 17:23:21',NULL,'decision','Corrected CLAUDE.md section 12 on 27 Aug 2026. It had said ''escapes and heredocs do not mix'' and that \b ''arrives as an actual backspace (0x08)''. Both wrong in ways that matter: the collapse is done by the Bash tool to the whole command string regardless of quoting, so a quoted heredoc is not the safe harbour the old wording implied, and the 0x08 is produced by the consuming language rather than the shell. Measured rather than reasoned. The same false mechanism appeared twice in the file and only one copy would have been fixed without looking for the second, which is that section''s own rule about copies.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(22,'2026-08-26 18:01:47',NULL,'decision','Fixed the quality findings in all three Magi Reader books on 27 Aug 2026 rather than only reporting them. Position bias was mechanical so it got a tool; the length tell was writing so 67 distractors were rewritten by hand. Added answerCycle to quality.js because the obvious fix for position bias (round-robin) produces a perfect even spread and a visible cycle that scores 100%, which the existing check would have called clean. The test asserting Magi WAS beatable was inverted rather than deleted, as its own comment asked.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(23,'2026-08-26 18:06:41',NULL,'error','snapshot.py''s first version decided whether to commit by comparing the copied files against their source. The dry run had already copied everything, so the --commit run found no difference and printed ''nothing changed, so nothing to commit'' against a repository with ZERO commits and ZERO tracked files. The skip condition was satisfiable by the commit having never happened, which is the exact failure class the repo was created to protect against. Fixed to ask git status --porcelain instead of the copy step. Caught only by checking rev-list --count afterwards rather than reading the reassuring message.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(24,'2026-08-26 18:08:40',NULL,'error','advised a bare git init on .claude, which would have staged nine .key files','Corrected by the Magi Reader session before Dan acted on it. The fix is an allowlist copy into dev/claude-config, not a denylist .gitignore: a denylist fails by leaking whatever nobody thought of, an allowlist fails by missing a file.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(25,'2026-08-26 18:13:14',NULL,'decision','Added a round-trip test to dev/claude-config on 27 Aug 2026: clone the repo and compare every restored file against its source in .claude. It found a real defect on its first run (the autocrlf rewrite) which four earlier checks had missed, because all of them asked whether the right things went IN and none asked whether they came back OUT unchanged. For a backup that is the only question that matters.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(26,'2026-08-26 18:20:52',NULL,'error','My repo sweep flagged 10 of 23 repos under dev/ as at risk. Six were false: gf-art, ghost-front, longnight, profile-readme, raven-classroom and world-aflame all differ from their remote HEAD, but GitHub HAS their local HEAD -- the remotes are simply ahead. The bug was folding ''could not determine'' into ''at risk'': rev-list could not count because the remote object was never fetched locally, and I printed ''?'' then treated it as a risk. That is the tri-state failure another session named earlier tonight, in my own tool, hours later. The right question is not ''are local and remote equal'' but ''does the remote CONTAIN the local HEAD'', answered by gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/commits/<sha>.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(27,'2026-08-26 18:23:45',NULL,'decision','hardened the gitleaks pre-commit template, left 23 existing repos alone','The old template failed open. New template falls back to PATH before refusing, and refuses loudly. Existing repos keep their copy: init.templateDir only applies at init/clone, and rewriting 23 hooks while five sessions are committing is a bigger risk than the latent one being fixed. Rollout is Dan''s call; the one-liner is in the report.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(28,'2026-08-26 18:27:01',NULL,'decision','Swept the machine for hook bypasses on 27 Aug 2026: git aliases global and per-repo, core.hooksPath, HUSKY env, shell profiles, and 292 scripts and package.json files under dev/ and magi-app. Zero instances of --no-verify. Proved the matcher fires first by planting two canaries (a .sh and a package.json) and confirming 2 of 2 hits, so the zero is a real zero rather than an unproven grep.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(29,'2026-08-26 18:37:37',NULL,'error','While testing the new magi-app pre-commit hook I put marker echoes at the top of it, staged a throwaway probe.txt, and committed to see which markers survived. The commit SUCCEEDED, because a file with no secret in it is supposed to pass, and my follow-up `git reset --soft HEAD` was a no-op that reset to the commit I had just made. A stray ''probe'' commit sat on master until I checked git log. Never pushed; undone with reset HEAD~1 and confirmed equal to origin/main again. The lesson is that a test which commits for real needs its undo written before the test runs, not after, and `reset --soft HEAD` is not an undo.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(30,'2026-08-27 00:09:23',NULL,'decision','Pushed Magi Reader 0.8.0 to itch on 27 Aug 2026 at dancockrell/the-gift-of-the-magi:html. No cleanup of old versions was needed or possible: Dan had already cleared the account, so the project had zero channels and this push created the first one. From here, pushing to html replaces that channel''s build, which is the discard-the-old behaviour he asked for. The legacy single-file prototype was built (magi-reader-0.8.0-legacy.zip, 745 files) but NOT pushed, since only the default channel is what visitors play and the prototype''s durable home is the git tag.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(31,'2026-08-27 00:18:28',NULL,'decision','Pushed both readers to itch on 27 Aug 2026: dancockrell/the-gift-of-the-magi:html at 0.8.0 (build #1919082) and dancockrell/the-raven-edgar-allen-poe:html at 1.0.0 (build #1919096). BOTH currently present as downloads rather than browser-playable, because itch only treats an html channel as playable when the project''s Kind of project is set to HTML, which is web-UI-only and butler cannot change. Flagged to Dan. Also flagged: the raven''s itch slug and page title spell it Edgar ALLEN Poe; the reader itself spells it correctly.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(32,'2026-08-27 02:36:43',NULL,'decision','Ported The Raven properly onto the magi-reader engine on 27 Aug 2026 after shipping the deprecated single-file build. Engine needed NO changes to read it, which is the claim src/books/index.js has been making since it was written. Three things went wrong first: media hand-copied (reproducible on one machine only), a plain build shipping the whole shelf (1,253 files carrying both titles), and pack-book.mjs missing passIntroRun so it would have deleted three pass introductions per book with every check passing. All three are now documented in docs/ADDING-A-BOOK.md and, where possible, enforced by registry.test.js. Store builds: The Raven 199 files 7.1 MB, Magi 387 files 16.4 MB.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(33,'2026-08-27 03:59:32',NULL,'install','OpenClaw 2026.7.1-2 installed globally via npm','npm install -g openclaw@latest --allow-scripts=openclaw. Binary at C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Roaming/npm/openclaw.cmd (npm prefix, NOT on Git Bash PATH by default). Config at C:/Users/Admin/.openclaw/openclaw.json. It is an MCP client, so local MCP servers register with ''openclaw mcp add NAME --command X --arg Y'' and verify with ''openclaw mcp probe''. Onboarding (messaging channels) was NOT run.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(34,'2026-08-27 04:00:52',NULL,'decision','Worked desktop-vision-rig issues on 27 Aug 2026. #13/#14 (duplicate CLI click crash) were already fixed; widened the AST signature test from browser+genie to every module cli.py imports, taking guarded call sites from 15 to 69, verified by injecting a bad kwarg into a scene call. #15 was marked closed but the fix could not detect the case it was filed for: {cache:''reload''} does not bypass a service worker. Fixed with a cache-busting query, moved the check onto the shot itself (a warning behind a command nobody types arrives after the damage), and added browser reload --hard as the way out. Commits 7f2901b and 69ea7d1, 92 tests.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(35,'2026-08-27 04:32:22',NULL,'milestone','VS 2022 repair running; MSVC CRT libs confirmed missing','Independently verified 2026-08-27: two elevated setup.exe processes started 11:29:50, and vcruntime.lib / oldnames.lib / legacy_stdio_definitions.lib are genuinely absent from VC/Tools/MSVC/14.40.33807/lib/x64 while 61 other .lib files remain. Native builds targeting msvc will fail to link until it finishes -- dr-companion is Tauri and therefore affected. Reported by the Claude scheduler session; claims held up.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(36,'2026-08-27 04:33:46',NULL,'install','Claude CLI @anthropic-ai/claude-code 2.1.247 installed globally and authenticated','Needed because OpenClaw''s --auth-choice anthropic-cli reads the Claude CLI''s own credentials, which are separate from the Claude Code desktop app. Verify with ''claude auth status'' (loggedIn true, authMethod claude.ai). First install exited 0 but skipped postinstall; reinstalled with --allow-scripts.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(37,'2026-08-27 04:33:46',NULL,'milestone','OpenClaw onboarded; Gateway running loopback-only on 127.0.0.1:18789','openclaw onboard --non-interactive --accept-risk --flow quickstart --auth-choice anthropic-cli --skip-channels --gateway-auth token --gateway-bind loopback --install-daemon. Installed as Scheduled Task ''OpenClaw Gateway''. No messaging channels connected. Verify: openclaw gateway status.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(38,'2026-08-27 04:42:39',NULL,'milestone','MSVC x64 CRT libs are present again mid-repair; vcvars64 sets LIB correctly','Measured 27 Aug 2026 ~11:55 while two elevated setup.exe VS repair processes were STILL RUNNING, so this is an in-flight snapshot and not a settled state. Three libs recorded as missing in trap/msvc-x64-crt-libs-missing (vcruntime.lib, oldnames.lib, legacy_stdio_definitions.lib) are all PRESENT, and lib/x64 holds 68 .lib files against the 64 implied by that entry. Separately, trap/vs-install-damaged-vcvars-silent says vcvars64.bat exits 0 while setting nothing: the stated MECHANISM is confirmed - ''where vswhere'' exits 1, so the VS Installer directory is genuinely not on PATH - but the CONSEQUENCE does not reproduce. Run through a CRLF batch file, vcvars64 gives vcvars_exit=0 with LIB=SET, INCLUDE=SET, VCTOOLS=SET. Do not read either trap as current until the repair finishes; run the checks instead. The check that settles the second one: call vcvars64.bat, then ''if defined LIB'' - never the exit code.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(39,'2026-08-27 04:43:30',NULL,'milestone','Visual Studio 2022 repaired; MSVC CRT libs restored and vcvars fixed','Repair restored vcruntime.lib, oldnames.lib, legacy_stdio_definitions.lib to lib/x64. Separately, vcvars'' vswhere failure was fixed by adding the VS Installer dir to the user PATH - the repair did not address that. Verified: clean cargo build + 35 tests with no crt-static and no onecore fallback; vcvars sets LIB standalone.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(40,'2026-08-27 04:48:04',NULL,'milestone','VS 2022 repair finished; native builds verified working','Installer exited, state settled. All three CRT libs present; .lib count in lib/x64 went 61 -> 68 -> 76 across three measurements tonight by three sessions, which is the clearest illustration available of why a claim about a disk under active repair cannot be recorded as a fact. vcvars64 now sets LIB, INCLUDE and VCToolsInstallDir. The vcvars fault was NEVER the repair''s to fix: vswhere.exe was off PATH, fixed by the scheduler session appending the VS Installer dir to USER PATH only - verified user scope, machine PATH untouched, no elevation used.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(41,'2026-08-27 05:15:27',NULL,'error','dev/magi-reader remote deleted; 174 art files backed up nowhere','Found by the Red Team GitHub session and verified here. Audio survives in the itch zip; the 174 webp art files do not exist anywhere else. Registered quartermaster capability ''git-remotes-alive'' running tools/check-git-remotes.sh, currently FAILING on dead=1.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(42,'2026-08-27 06:59:25',NULL,'decision','dr-companion: column widths are stored as intent and bounded at the point of use, never clamped on write. src/lib/columns.ts does the arithmetic once for map, dashboard and room together - the room column is guaranteed a floor because it holds the game text, input and channel tabs, and the other two scale together when a window cannot honour both. Two earlier shapes were wrong and both were caught by measuring the running app rather than reading the source: no ceiling at all (map 1201.6px in an 1180px window put every game control 490-718px off an edge that does not scroll), and a per-column ceiling that left 420px ''for the rest'' while the dashboard held all 420 of them.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(43,'2026-08-27 07:41:00',NULL,'milestone','OpenClaw Discord channel configured but NOT connected (4014)','Plugin installed, bot app created (@Open Claw - Project 42, id 1542429121173266433), token valid and stored as USER env DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN. Blocked on two things that are Dan''s: enable Message Content + Server Members privileged intents, and invite the bot to a server. Least-privilege invite URL uses permissions=309237763136. Telegram and LINE plugins installed but unconfigured; LINE additionally needs a public HTTPS webhook which loopback binding cannot provide.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(44,'2026-08-27 07:57:43',NULL,'decision','dr-companion: Lich install now functional on this machine (27 Aug 2026) - gems installed (sqlite3, ox, gtk3 + deps via ridk install 1 3 for the MSYS2 toolchain), 24 missing source files restored from v5.20.1 release, launch_lich fixed to use --stormfront --headless=11024 instead of bare --genie. Dan is mid-login in Lich''s own Manual Entry tab (DragonRealms/Phemius, ''Save this info'' checked) as of this session - has not yet clicked Play. Once saved, the app''s ''Open Lich to sign in'' -> character button flow should work end to end.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(45,'2026-08-27 08:03:35',NULL,'error','Files >64KB disappearing machine-wide; CCleaner is prime suspect','348 cargo crates compared against their archives: 2 files missing, both >64KB, none under. Dirs timestamped 26 Aug 16:10. CCleaner started 26 Aug 15:42. Same 64KB threshold independently found in the Lich5 tree (24 files). OneDrive, disk health and Defender ruled out.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(46,'2026-08-27 08:49:35',NULL,'milestone','Discord channel LIVE: sessions can post to RedWizard''s Clawjam #general','Verified by actually posting three messages, not by reading a status line. Bot @Open Claw - Project 42 connected, privileged intents enabled, in the server with admin. Route: openclaw message send --channel discord --target channel:1542447962926489653 -m ''...''');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(47,'2026-08-27 09:06:26',NULL,'milestone','Recovered 177 deleted tracked files across 4 repos','All >64KB, restored byte-exact from local git objects and verified by hash. gf-art 70, magi-reader 94, longnight 11, world-aflame 2. They were UNCOMMITTED deletions, so a git add -A by any session would have made them permanent and pushed them. magi-reader matters most: its remote is deleted, so local git objects were the only copy.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(48,'2026-08-27 09:11:18',NULL,'milestone','deletion event confirmed over; all tracked files restored','Swept 28 repos under dev/: ZERO tracked-but-missing files and every object store passes fsck. magi-reader independently re-verified at 748/748 present with all 743 media blobs readable from the object store - earlier tonight I measured 94 of them missing from disk and did not recognise it as the same event. Recovery worked ONLY because git held the files. The exposure that remains is everything git cannot help with: the three ownerless Godot projects in Documents (388 files, 23 MB, NO git at all, newest file 2026-08-14) and four repos with no off-machine remote.');
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(49,'2026-08-27 09:29:00',NULL,'decision','dr-companion: Python scripting layer built and working end-to-end (27 Aug 2026). Out-of-process, decided - a script is its own process talking to src-tauri/src/script_api.rs over a loopback JSON-line socket (token-authed, same threat model as companion_bridge.lic''s token). python/dr_companion.py is the pure-stdlib client library. Verified against the real running app + real replay fixture: real game lines (with seq numbers) flowed through Rust''s game_link.rs -> script_api.rs broadcast -> Python callback. Known gap, documented not hidden: scripts get raw tagged wire text (<pushStream> markup included) because gameStream.ts''s tag parser exists only in TypeScript and porting it untested to Rust/Python risked a second parser silently disagreeing with the first. See docs/PYTHON_API.md and docs/ENGINE.md.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(50,'2026-08-27 10:09:55',NULL,'milestone','Magi and Raven published as live GitHub Pages demos, linked from each repo''s homepage field',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(51,'2026-08-27 10:32:26',NULL,'milestone','Fixed two dead engine features found by live play: per-pass Wren intros (passIntroRun never called), per-line pictures for Raven (120 beat images extracted but never mapped). Rebuilt+republished both Pages demos; removed Raven''s legacy standalone build entirely.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(52,'2026-08-27 15:35:04',NULL,'decision','dr-companion sound alerts were silently broken: GamePane.tsx''s alert-sound useEffect depended on [lines, highlights] where lines=gameLines() returns the same mutated-in-place array reference forever (documented in gameLink.ts''s gameVersion() comment as the exact defect that silenced the channel tabs). React never saw lines change, so playAlert() never fired for real game text after mount, even though the whole pipeline (highlight match -> paint -> playAlert -> read_sound -> Audio.play) worked perfectly when invoked directly. Fixed 27 Aug 2026 by keying the effect on version (gameVersion()''s counter) instead of lines. Verified against fake-lich.mjs fixture: 0 plays in 20s before the fix, 11 real Audio.play() calls in 20s after. This is the third place this exact defect class has recurred in this codebase.',NULL);
INSERT INTO "events" VALUES(53,'2026-08-27 16:06:46',NULL,'milestone','Chrome repaired: only chrome.exe and chrome_proxy.exe were missing','Second occurrence today. Diagnosed rather than reinstalled: 270 of 272 files present, chrome.dll 298MB intact, profile 4.9GB untouched. MSI repair restored exactly the two files and Chrome runs. Defender, size-based deletion and interrupted-update artefacts all ruled out by measurement.');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(1,'trap','vram-wmi','Win32_VideoController.AdapterRAM reports the RTX 4070 as 4 GB (32-bit overflow). Use nvidia-smi.','verified','2026-08-23','2026-08-26 15:29:46','2026-08-26 15:29:46',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(2,'trap','crlf-scripts','Heredocs write LF; cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only scripts with misleading errors. Fix with sed then verify with cat -A.','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:29:46','2026-08-26 15:29:46',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(3,'trap','temp-wipe','Never clear TEMP wholesale on a running system. Broke a Chrome update mid-flight, removing chrome.exe while 268 files stayed intact.','verified','2026-08-26','2026-08-26 15:29:46','2026-08-26 15:29:46',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(4,'trap','git-noreply','Commits must use the GitHub noreply email or pushes are rejected, and the error does not say so.','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:29:46','2026-08-26 15:29:46',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(5,'trap','exec-policy','LocalMachine execution policy is AllSigned, blocking npm.ps1. npm works in Git Bash and cmd.','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:29:46','2026-08-26 15:29:46',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(6,'tool','gpu','RTX 4070, 12012 MB VRAM. Models above ~12 GB spill to shared memory.','verified','2026-08-23','2026-08-26 15:29:46','2026-08-26 15:29:46',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(7,'trap','file-stripping','Something on this machine strips large files out of untracked dependency trees, and not only in Downloads. 26 Aug 2026: between two runs of the same suite half an hour apart, Downloads/testgrader/tools/node_modules/playwright-core went from a working install to 733 KB with every .js bundle gone and only LICENSE files left, and icudtl.dat disappeared from AppData/Local/ms-playwright/chromium_headless_shell-1234, so Chrome launched and died with ''Invalid file descriptor to ICU data received'' while --version still worked. Git-tracked files were untouched. Recovery: remove node_modules entirely and reinstall (a plain npm install says ''up to date'' from the lockfile without checking file contents, so it does nothing), then npx playwright install chromium --force. Treat an inexplicable module-not-found, or a browser that starts and then dies, as this before suspecting code.','verified','quickgrade-session','2026-08-26T22:52:38','2026-08-26T22:52:38',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(8,'trap','python-none-on-path','There is no working ''python'' on PATH. python and python3 both resolve to the Windows Store aliases in AppData/Local/Microsoft/WindowsApps, which advertise the Store and exit without executing anything. ''py'' is not installed. The conda install at C:/Users/Admin/anaconda3/python.exe starts under a conda shell but NOT from a child process (it fails with ''Could not find platform independent libraries'') because it needs its own directories on PATH for its DLLs. The one that works from anything is C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Programs/Python/Python313/python.exe, 3.13.15. Any script that shells out to Python must probe a candidate with -c print(1) rather than trust a name, or the fact that a file exists on disk.','verified','quickgrade-session','2026-08-26T22:52:38','2026-08-26T22:52:38',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(9,'trap','pip-broken','pip on the Python313 install is itself damaged: ''No module named pip._vendor.rich._emoji_codes''. python -m ensurepip --upgrade does not repair it, because ensurepip reads the recorded version, sees pip present and stops. Same family as the file-stripping trap. Consequence: no pip installs on that interpreter until it is repaired, so plan around it rather than through it. Reading a PDF, for instance, was done by rendering it with pdf.js inside headless Chromium instead of installing pypdf.','verified','quickgrade-session','2026-08-26T22:52:38','2026-08-26T22:52:38',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(11,'trap','crlf-breaks-anchors','Repos here are checked out with CRLF endings, so a patch script that matches a multi-line anchor joined with newline finds nothing, makes no change, and reports success. Detect the ending first and build anchors with it, or splice by line number. This wasted several rounds before it was noticed, because every symptom looked like a wrong anchor string.','verified','quickgrade-session','2026-08-26T22:52:38','2026-08-26T22:52:38',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(12,'trap','cuda-dll-path','pip nvidia-* wheels put DLLs in site-packages/nvidia/*/bin. os.add_dll_directory is NOT enough - CTranslate2 resolves cuBLAS via its own LoadLibrary. Prepend those dirs to os.environ PATH before importing faster_whisper. Symptom: Library cublas64_12.dll is not found.','verified','2026-08-23','2026-08-26 15:53:01','2026-08-26 15:53:01',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(13,'trap','uv-python-312','uv venv --python 3.12 fails with a spurious ''missing expected target directory'' error. Pass the interpreter path directly instead.','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:53:01','2026-08-26 15:53:01',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(14,'trap','winget-fresh-terminal','winget-installed binaries do not resolve until a NEW terminal opens. They live under AppData/Local/Microsoft/WinGet/Packages/<Publisher.Name>_<hash>/','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:53:01','2026-08-26 15:53:01',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(15,'trap','ollama-app-supervises','Killing ''ollama app'' kills the server - the desktop app supervises ''ollama serve'' and port 11434 goes with it.','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:53:01','2026-08-26 15:53:01',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(16,'trap','rust-not-on-path','Rust 1.98.0 is installed at %USERPROFILE%/.cargo but is NOT on PATH in Git Bash. Tauri builds need it.','verified','2026-08-26','2026-08-26 15:53:02','2026-08-26 15:53:02',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(17,'trap','transcript-no-speaker','search_session_transcripts returns user messages, assistant messages and tool output undifferentiated. Never attribute a snippet without checking who produced it.','verified','2026-08-25','2026-08-26 15:53:02','2026-08-26 15:53:02',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(18,'trap','verify-outcome-not-output','gh repo create --push prints the repo URL whether or not the push succeeded. Verify state via API, never stdout. Cost: 11 repos reported pushed while empty, 3 times.','verified','2026-08-24','2026-08-26 15:53:02','2026-08-26 15:53:02',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(19,'feedback','publish-voice','Anything Dan publishes under his own name: no em dashes or middle-dot separators, no delve/leverage/robust/seamless, no reflexive three-item lists. His audience (educators) is the most AI-text-fatigued group in the workforce.','verified','2026-08-25','2026-08-26 15:53:02','2026-08-26 15:53:02',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(20,'feedback','claim-standard','Only claim what survives an unannounced test. Dan''s own rule, applied to his languages and skills. Applies to READMEs, commit messages and status reports too.','verified','2026-08-25','2026-08-26 15:53:02','2026-08-26 15:53:02',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(21,'trap','npm-test-fail-grep-is-unsound','Counting "^FAIL" lines in npm test output reports 0 failures when a suite CRASHES rather than fails. dr-companion without Ruby on PATH: exit code 1, 313 OK lines, 0 FAIL lines - 90 assertions never ran and the check said clean. Read the exit code. This was used repeatedly before it was caught.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:53:34','2026-08-26 15:53:34',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(22,'trap','heredoc-escapes-arrive-mangled','An escape written through a shell heredoc does not survive. \b arrives as an actual backspace (0x08), \s as plain s. The regex still compiles and matches nothing, so it looks like empty data rather than a broken pattern. Hit three times in one session with the trap already documented. Use the file-edit tool for anything containing escapes and verify with charCodeAt.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:53:34','2026-08-26 15:53:34',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(23,'trap','deleting-unused-data-is-an-invisible-bet','Deleting a derived artefact that nothing currently reads is a bet that no future feature needs it. The bet is invisible when made and silent when lost. The art daemon deleted each evaluation thumbnail after scoring it - obviously correct, small files, already consumed - and when the scoring scale turned out to be wrong, 172 renders could not be re-measured. Ask what would need this if the thing that produced it were wrong.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:53:34','2026-08-26 15:53:34',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(24,'trap','old-data-under-a-new-meaning','Values stored under a key whose meaning later changes are the quietest bug available: nothing errors and every number looks plausible. Measures saved as "stdev" meant raw pixels; the next version read the same key as contrast-normalised. Clear stale values rather than converting them - a converted number carries the same false confidence and is harder to spot. Same shape as a schema change CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS silently skips.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:53:34','2026-08-26 15:53:34',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(25,'project','dr-companion-art-pack-size','17,750 room images at a mean 178 KB is about 3.0 GB, against a 72 MB repository. public/rooms is gitignored and needs a release-asset distribution path (issue #8). Creatures (773) and portraits (22) ARE committed at 53 MB because every card and character sheet needs them.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:53:34','2026-08-26 15:53:34',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(26,'trap','flux-dev-removed','FLUX.1-dev (non-commercial) was deleted from ComfyUI models on 2026-08-26. Only flux1-schnell-fp8 (Apache-2.0) remains, which is what dr-companion pins. Do not reinstall dev - it would make generated art packs legally unusable.','verified','2026-08-26','2026-08-26 15:56:40','2026-08-26 15:56:40',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(27,'trap','fail-line-counting','Counting FAIL lines in test output is unsound. dr-companion without Ruby: exit code 1, 313 passing assertions, ZERO FAIL lines, 90 assertions never ran. Read the exit code, not the output. Generalises rule 1.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:56:40','2026-08-26 15:56:40',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(28,'feedback','colocate-warnings','A shared database helps a session that thinks to query it. A README in the directory reaches whoever is standing there deciding what to delete. Both are needed; the second is the one that catches an outsider. Put the warning where the mistake would happen.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 15:56:40','2026-08-26 15:56:40',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(29,'feedback','warning-placement','The warning goes where the DESTRUCTIVE ACTION happens - not where the dependency is declared, not where a careful reader would look. A project README reaches someone reading the project. It does not reach someone standing in C:\Ruby4Lich5 deciding if that folder is clutter. Use ''mem guard'' to write WHAT-USES-THIS.md into the dependency''s own directory.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:01:09','2026-08-26 16:01:09',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(30,'trap','stale-warning-worse-than-none','A warning describing a situation that has changed is worse than no warning: it spends the reader''s attention and teaches them the file is stale. Regenerate co-located warnings from the DB rather than hand-maintaining them.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:01:09','2026-08-26 16:01:09',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(31,'trap','burst-vs-recurring','visual-rig ''recurring'' flags a run of events sharing one timestamp as STILL GOING. 14 dr-companion warnings all stamped 22:51:49 were a single injection, not an ongoing fault. Events sharing one timestamp are a burst - needs a rule.','reported','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:01:09','2026-08-26 16:01:09',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(32,'trap','PYTHON_ON_PATH_IS_A_STUB','python.exe on PATH is the Windows Store alias at AppData\Local\Microsoft\WindowsApps and fails with ''the file cannot be accessed by the system''. The real interpreter is C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\Programs\Python\Python313\python.exe. There is no py launcher.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(33,'trap','POWERSHELL_APOSTROPHE_IN_LEGACY_PATH','The magi-app repo lives under a folder literally named ''Legacy builds and Assets...if you can''''t find something, try here''. The apostrophe in can''''t breaks every single-quoted PowerShell string and every inline node -e that embeds the path. Use a script file and pass the path as an argument, or Join-Path with a variable. This broke four separate commands in one session.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(34,'trap','NODE_INLINE_EVAL_MANGLES_REGEX','node -e through PowerShell mangles backticks, dollar signs and backslashes, so regex literals and template strings arrive corrupted. A .mjs file run by path is the only reliable route. Symptom: ''Unterminated regexp literal'' or a replacement that silently matches nothing.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(35,'trap','RAVEN_AUDIO_LIVES_IN_ZIPS','The Raven''s 368 narration mp3s and its word-level timings.js were only ever inside raven-itch-folder.zip / _2 / _4 / _6 beside the magi-app folder. They are now committed to dancockrell/the-raven-edgar-allan-poe-magi-reader under pack/audio and pack/cues. Before deleting any raven-itch-folder zip, confirm that repo still has 368 files in pack/audio.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(36,'trap','MAGI_MEDIA_IS_SPREAD_ACROSS_FOLDERS','No single folder holds a complete set of Magi''s art. magi-itch-ui has 29 of 54 plates, magi-itch-guide2-clean 20, magi-itch-improved 13. Only the union is whole, which is why tools/copy-assets.mjs now searches seven sources and takes the union instead of naming one folder.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(37,'trap','PLAYWRIGHT_ITCH_TEST_NEEDS_ITS_OWN_RUN','magi-app''s e2e/itch.spec.js stands up two extra HTTP servers and loads the built game in an iframe. Under four workers it times out even at 90s; alone it takes 12.6s. Tagged @serial, run by npm run e2e:serial, and verify:full runs it FIRST because running it after the parallel suite fails on a warm machine. Do not answer this by raising the timeout again; that was tried twice.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(38,'trap','MAGI_APP_IS_BACKED_UP','magi-app in the Legacy folder DOES have a remote: github.com/dancockrell/magi-reader-engine, branch master pushing to main, 44 commits, clean. A report that it has no remote and zero commits was wrong, probably from running git in the wrong directory. Verify with git config --get remote.origin.url before ''rescuing'' it.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:02:25','2026-08-26 16:02:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(39,'feedback','generated-warnings-need-correct-source','Generating a warning file from a database is right - it cannot drift - but it only moves the accuracy problem to the row. Two of the dr-companion rows were wrong within an hour: one said the project ''works alongside'' Genie when it only reads its map files, and one said FLUX.1-dev was on this machine after it had been deleted. Fix the row, not the file. And treat a thin row as a bug, because the generated file can only be as specific as its source.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:03:10','2026-08-26 16:03:10',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(40,'trap','git-audit-branch-mismatch','My repo audit reported magi-app as having 0 commits and no remote. Wrong: it is dancockrell/magi-reader-engine with 44 commits, clean. The bug was mine - I computed unpushed as ''origin/$branch..HEAD'' using the LOCAL branch name. magi-app is master locally pushing to main, so origin/master does not exist and the check silently returned nothing. Compare against the remote''s actual default branch.','verified','2026-08-26','2026-08-26 16:05:55','2026-08-26 16:05:55',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(41,'trap','silent-skip-hides-gaps','A skip counted as housekeeping hides real gaps. mem guard reported ''7 skipped (URLs and non-directories)'' while the FLUX licence dependency - the one with a legal consequence - had no warning file anywhere. Skips must be loud and itemised.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:05:55','2026-08-26 16:05:55',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(42,'trap','generated-from-bad-row','Generating a warning from a database moves the accuracy problem to the row, it does not remove it. The file cannot drift from the row; the row can still be wrong or thin. A one-line ''why'' produces a warning nobody stops for - same defect as an empty warning, harder to see.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:05:55','2026-08-26 16:05:55',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(43,'trap','legacy-folder-apostrophe','The Legacy folder name contains an apostrophe ("...if you can''t find something..."). It breaks every single-quoted PowerShell string and every inline node -e touching that path. Use double quotes or a variable.','verified','magi-reader-session','2026-08-26 16:05:55','2026-08-26 16:05:55',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(45,'trap','negative-result-vs-absent-result','The commonest bug across three sessions in one day: a check reports success because it never ran. A negative result and an absent result are indistinguishable unless you make them different. Four instances, all silent: counting FAIL lines in a suite that crashed (exit 1, zero FAIL lines, 90 assertions never run); asserting none of these prompts are missing the clause against an EMPTY file (all 0 carry it, passed - and that is the gate that runs first to stop a nudity regression); a dependency guard reporting 7 skipped where the skips WERE the unprotected paths; a git check against origin/master in a repo pushing to main. Fix: prove the work happened. Read exit codes. Assert a floor on how many things were checked, set well below the real count. Print the count. Make skips loud and non-zero-exit.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:09:32','2026-08-26 16:09:32',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(46,'trap','negative-vs-absent-result','A negative result and an absent result print identically unless you make them different, and the absent one looks like success. Four instances in one session: safety-test.mjs passed against an empty prompt file; a FAIL-line count reported clean on a crashed suite; mem guard reported ''0 written'' against a wiped dependencies table; a git audit reported ''no remote'' when origin/$branch did not exist. Fix: assert the denominator is non-empty and print what was checked.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:12:15','2026-08-26 16:12:15',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(47,'feedback','denominator-must-be-the-fragile-thing','Count the check against the thing that goes to zero when the mechanism fails, not the thing that stays constant. ''No humanoid is undressed'' is true and meaningless if the humanoid detector classified nothing. Denominator = humanoids found, not creatures total.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:12:15','2026-08-26 16:12:15',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(48,'feedback','rules-recognise-they-do-not-prevent','Writing a rule down does not create the reflex. In one session I wrote ''verify the outcome not the output'' then broke it twice more; DR Companion wrote ''a stale warning is worse than none'' then left one for an hour. What actually caught both was another session inspecting the artefact. Rules help recognise a failure that is already in front of you. Cross-checking is what prevents it.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:12:15','2026-08-26 16:12:15',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(49,'reference','witness-chain-renamed','witness-chain was renamed to project-42-blockchain. Repo: dancockrell/project-42-blockchain. Any earlier reference to witness-chain means this.','verified','downloads-f5','2026-08-26 16:17:49','2026-08-26 16:17:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(50,'trap','dual-signature-collusion','Dual-signature verification does not prevent collusion. Two cooperating signers can co-sign each other''s records indefinitely and dominate aggregate statistics (win-rate mining) without ever failing verification. Any consumer aggregating across a chain needs a DISTINCT-COSIGNER count, not a signature count. Raised against project-42-blockchain issue #1 by the World Aflame session.','verified','downloads-f5','2026-08-26 16:17:49','2026-08-26 16:17:49',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(51,'trap','pipe-discards-exit-code','A shell pipeline reports the exit status of its LAST command. So `cmd 2>&1 | tail -1 || fallback` never runs the fallback, because tail always succeeds. Every git push in one dr-companion session used that pattern and the rebase fallback was dead code across 22 commits. It cost nothing only because the real check was comparing local and origin SHAs afterwards. Redirect to a file and test $?, or set pipefail. Two sessions hit this independently on 26 Aug 2026.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:18:08','2026-08-26 16:18:08',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(52,'trap','generated-file-not-regenerated','Generating a doc from a database removes drift only while something re-runs the generator. dr-companion DEPENDENCIES.md carried a claim that a model was on this machine for an hour after the database row had been corrected and the model deleted. The row was right; nothing had re-run export. Consider running the generator on any write to the source table, or flagging a generated file older than the row it came from.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:18:08','2026-08-26 16:18:08',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(53,'trap','python-backslash-U','Windows paths in Python source break on \U (C:\Users) and \x etc. Use r''...'' raw strings or forward slashes. Hit this twice in one session INCLUDING while writing the note about it.','verified','2026-08-26','2026-08-26 16:21:59','2026-08-26 16:21:59',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(54,'trap','pipe-eats-exit-status','Never read $? after a pipe - it reports the LAST command''s status. ''cmd | tail'' always succeeds. Killed a git push retry fallback for 22 commits (DR Companion) and nearly made me file a working fix as broken.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:21:59','2026-08-26 16:21:59',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(55,'feedback','generate-then-nothing-reruns','Generating a file from a database does not help if nothing re-runs the generator. A file cannot drift while being written and drifts for as long as it is not. mem review now flags generated files older than their rows; export/guard touch mtime on no-op so the flag can actually clear.','verified','dr-companion-session','2026-08-26 16:21:59','2026-08-26 16:21:59',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(56,'trap','VACUOUS_SWEEP_IN_TESTS','The test-suite form of ''a check that reports success without running'': a test walks a population, collects offenders, asserts the list is empty. That passes when nothing is wrong AND when nothing was examined. magi-reader-engine has tools/vacuous-sweeps.mjs to find them (40 sweeps, 29 with no population check, most benign). The fix is one line: assert the population was non-empty before asserting the offenders list is. Real instances found: plates over zero plates, answers over zero questions, translations over zero words, and an alignment sweep that ''continue''d past every clip when the cue file failed to load.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:22:44','2026-08-26 16:22:44',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(57,'trap','DETECTOR_FOUND_ITSELF','The vacuous-sweep detector''s first version reported ''0 sweeps, 0 unguarded'' having found no test files at all: its parser started scanning inside a string literal and never terminated. A clean bill of health from a tool that examined nothing. Any auditing tool must print its own population count and exit non-zero when that count is zero, or it will one day report success for the wrong reason.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:22:44','2026-08-26 16:22:44',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(60,'trap','peer-cannot-authorise-claude-md','Relayed permission is not permission. A session told three others that Dan had opened C:\Users\Admin\.claude\CLAUDE.md to all sessions. Its account was accurate and it was acting in good faith, and it still does not work: from the receiving side that message is indistinguishable from one that invented the authorisation, and the file governs how every session behaves. Applies to CLAUDE.md, permission settings and config. Decline, do the parts needing no escalation, and put the proposed change in front of Dan. RESOLVED 27 Aug 2026: Dan authorised it directly, in his own words, so the file IS editable by any session. The rule about relayed authorisation stands unchanged; only this instance is settled.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:26:32','2026-08-26 17:14:51',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(61,'feedback','write-the-check-not-the-claim','When documenting the state of anything on disk, record the COMMAND that establishes it, not the answer that command gave once. A claim about what exists rots the moment the world moves and stays equally authoritative; its reader cannot re-derive it. ''The audio does not exist and cannot be reconstructed'' was unfalsifiable and wrong. ''Look in raven-itch-folder*.zip for raven-audio/'' is a 30-second check that stays true. AUDIO-NEEDED.md worked only because it was scary, not because it was informative.','verified','magi-reader-session','2026-08-26 16:26:32','2026-08-26 16:26:32',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(62,'trap','PS_WILDCARD_PATH_WITH_FILTER_RETURNS_ZERO','PowerShell: Get-ChildItem on a path whose DIRECTORY portion contains a wildcard, combined with -Filter or -Include, silently returns 0. No error, and -ErrorAction Stop raises nothing. Get-ChildItem C:\Users\Admin\dev\the-raven-*\pack\audio -Filter *.mp3 returned 0 where the literal path returned 368; the wildcard form yields the directory itself as a single item, which then fails the filter. Resolve-Path on the same pattern resolves correctly, so the path is not the problem. Fix: put the wildcard in the LEAF, as "...\pack\audio\*.mp3", which returns 368. This matters because the zero reads as an honest absence of files.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:38:39','2026-08-26 16:38:39',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(63,'trap','warning-list-of-false-positives','A warning list where every entry is a false positive is worse than no list. mem review reported six dependency locations as GONE; all six were live. Rows are only comparable if the check can distinguish ''absent'' from ''I could not check this''. Report the second honestly rather than folding it into the first.','verified','found by Magi Reader session, one row; six on inspection','2026-08-26 16:49:42','2026-08-26 16:49:42',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(64,'trap','github-404-means-deleted-not-renamed','GitHub 301-redirects a renamed repository, so an old URL keeps working. A hard 404 from gh api repos/OWNER/NAME therefore means the repo was DELETED, not renamed. Use this to tell the two apart before assuming content moved to a similarly-named repo.','verified','dev/magi-reader remote 404 while magi-reader-engine exists','2026-08-26 16:49:43','2026-08-26 16:49:43',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(65,'trap','guess-last-look-first','Order heuristics after facts. classify_location used a '' and '' substring to detect prose, which matched a real directory named ''Legacy builds and Assets...'' and demoted a checkable path to unchecked. Ask the filesystem first; apply guesswork only to strings that already failed to resolve.','verified','self-inflicted while fixing warning-list-of-false-positives','2026-08-26 16:49:43','2026-08-26 16:49:43',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(66,'project','magi-media-single-copy','The magi book media (224 art + 519 audio = 743 files, 27.5 MB) is committed only to C:\Users\Admin\dev\magi-reader, whose GitHub remote dancockrell/magi-reader was DELETED (hard 404). magi-reader-engine holds 5 media files, all under docs/; magi-reader-classroom-toolkit holds 0. That working tree also has 94 uncommitted files. One disk, no remote. Dan''s call whether to publish.','verified','gh api git/trees recursive on all three repos, 2026-08-26','2026-08-26 16:49:43','2026-08-26 16:49:43',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(67,'trap','dead-remote-reports-in-sync','A git repo whose GitHub remote was DELETED reports itself as fully pushed, because every local answer comes from the cached remote-tracking ref and nothing contacts the server. Demonstrated in C:\Users\Admin\dev\magi-reader on 26 Aug 2026, whose remote 404s: rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD says 0; rev-parse origin/main resolves; branch -vv prints [origin/main] as if tracking is healthy; and status -sb prints ''## main...origin/main'' with no ahead/behind marker, which is exactly what a synced repo prints. The commands that DO fail are git ls-remote --exit-code origin and git fetch --dry-run origin, both exit 128. So never read an unpushed count on its own: ask ls-remote first, and treat the count as meaningless if it fails. This is how 743 files read as backed up while existing on one disk. See [[github-404-means-deleted-not-renamed]] for telling deletion from a rename: GitHub 301-redirects a renamed repo forever, so a hard 404 means deleted.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:51:35','2026-08-26 16:51:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(68,'trap','denominator-wider-than-the-claim','Counting evidence over a population broader than the claim makes an unbacked thing look backed up. Caught in my own verify-media.sh before it shipped: it summed ''.mp3'' across all three magi-reader repos to answer ''is The Gift of the Magi backed up'', so The Raven''s 368 narration files counted toward Magi''s total and it printed ''368 on GitHub'' for a book with zero files on GitHub. The fix is to partition by source and count by PATH, not by extension: grep for public/art and public/magi-audio specifically. Same shape as the four-checks-four-wrong list from the same hour. Ask what number goes to zero when the specific claim is false, and count that. Sibling of the rule that a check must assert its own population; this is the case where the population is real but belongs to something else.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 16:51:35','2026-08-26 16:51:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(69,'reference','witness-chain-godot-ledger','Reusable dual-signature tamper-evident event ledger for Godot 4, MIT, at github.com/dancockrell/project-42-blockchain. Drop witness_chain/ into any Godot 4 project. No server, no cryptocurrency, no proof-of-work; two independent RSA signatures per record via Godot''s Crypto class, hash-linked as a DAG so concurrent branches merge without arbitration. Transport-agnostic: no networking code included. Built by the World Aflame session; world-aflame-godot uses it for replay-verified Elo. Verified on the remote 2026-08-27: 19 blobs, 4 commits, MIT, README present.','verified','gh api git/trees recursive, not the announcement','2026-08-26 17:13:45','2026-08-26 17:13:45',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(70,'tool','claude-md-xref-checker','C:/Users/Admin/.claude/check-xrefs.py resolves every ''section N (hint)'' and ''rule N'' pointer in CLAUDE.md against the real headings and fails when a hint names a different rule. Built by the Magi Reader session; extended by the memory-db session to cover ''rule N'' and both letter cases, which doubled coverage from 7 references to 14. Its own proof is test-xrefs.py: 7 cases, 5 requiring a non-zero exit, run against temp copies so the live file is never mutated. Run both after editing CLAUDE.md.','verified','ran both; demonstrated failure in all five directions','2026-08-26 17:14:51','2026-08-26 17:20:21',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(71,'tool','visual-rig-sees-top-layer-elements','REASONED, NOT OBSERVED. visual-rig should capture <dialog> and [popover] content, because it grabs the composited desktop framebuffer via mss: no DOM, no render tree, no accessibility API in the path, and a browser paints top-layer elements into its own window surface before that surface reaches the compositor. Same argument covers native menus, tooltips and OS overlays, which DOM-based tools cannot reach. The author''s empirical test was INVALID (the probe page was not focused, so the capture recorded a different window, and even ordinary page text came back missing) and they reported that rather than the conclusion. The real limitation is different and confirmed: the rig only sees what composites to a display, so an app rendering in a pane that never composites is invisible to it regardless. That is issue #9. TO VERIFY: open the reader with a dialog showing and in front, then visual-rig clip --window "<title>" -l "dialog open" and visual-rig ask "<string only the dialog shows>" --annotate.','inferred',NULL,'2026-08-26 17:20:09','2026-08-26 17:20:09',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(73,'trap','ls-remote-before-counting-unpushed','Wording tweak, no --check passed.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 17:21:12','2026-08-27 09:43:25','git -C C:/Users/Admin/dev/magi-reader ls-remote --exit-code origin   # EXPECT 128');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(74,'trap','bash-tool-eats-one-backslash','SHARPENED 27 Aug 2026, superseding bash-tool-heredoc-eats-one-backslash and the backslash half of heredoc-backslash, both of which named the wrong culprit. It is NOT heredoc-specific and quoting does not protect you: the Bash tool halves every backslash run in the command string before bash parses it. Measured with od -c: ''A\\B'' in SINGLE QUOTES arrives as ''A\B'', and bash''s own argv confirms it received the collapsed form, though POSIX says single quotes are literal. Inside <<''EOF'' likewise, where POSIX guarantees no processing at all. Single backslashes survive; runs are halved. Type 2N to get N. SECOND HALF: the 0x08 usually blamed on the shell comes from the LANGUAGE. Writing a doubled-backslash-b into a .js file leaves a single-backslash-b on disk, and JavaScript reads that as a backspace (charCodeAt(0) === 8, length 1), so both spellings produce byte-identical files. The distinction is gone before the language sees it, which is why the regex compiles and matches nothing instead of erroring. REMEDY: use Write/Edit for any file containing a backslash, or drop the escapes entirely (forward slashes work in Windows paths in Python, JS and Git Bash). Verify with od -c or charCodeAt, never by eye. See also [[bash-tool-truncates-long-heredocs]] and [[python-backslash-U]].','verified','measured 27 Aug 2026 by the magi-reader session with od -c and bash argv','2026-08-26 17:23:21','2026-08-26 17:24:57','printf ''%s'' ''A\\B'' | od -c    -- output ''A \ B'' means the trap is LIVE (one backslash survived of two, inside single quotes, where POSIX says both are literal). Output ''A \ \ B'' means the tool no longer collapses and this row is stale.');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(75,'project','claude-config-unversioned','C:/Users/Admin/.claude is not a git repository and must not become one (see trap/claude-dir-holds-credentials). Hand-written substance is now snapshotted by allowlist into C:/Users/Admin/dev/claude-config: 41 files, CLAUDE.md + the two xref checkers + 32 memory markdown files, zero credential-shaped files tracked, verified clean by gitleaks AND an independent shape scan with a canary proving the scan fires. Built by the Magi Reader session. STILL HAS NO REMOTE - it holds Dan''s personal working notes, so pushing it is his call and private if anything.','verified','gitleaks 0 leaks over 41 files; shape scan 0 hits; canary detected','2026-08-26 17:23:49','2026-08-26 18:08:40','git -C C:/Users/Admin/dev/claude-config ls-files | grep -c ''\.key$''   # expect 0');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(76,'trap','bash-tool-truncates-long-heredocs','Long heredocs through the Bash tool are truncated before their terminator. It surfaces as ''unexpected EOF while looking for matching'' and then silently runs NOTHING in the entire command, including any earlier commands on the same line, which is the dangerous part: a multi-step command reports failure for the last step while none of the earlier steps ran either. Write files in chunks under about 120 lines, or use the Write tool, which has no such limit. Separate failure mode from [[bash-tool-eats-one-backslash]]; both were filed together as ''heredoc-backslash'' and only the backslash half was superseded. Observed by the quickgrade session 26 Aug 2026; carried forward without re-measurement.','reported','quickgrade-session, via heredoc-backslash before consolidation','2026-08-26 17:24:57','2026-08-26 17:24:57',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(77,'trap','genie-plugin-sees-server-text-only','The Genie CompanionBridge plugin (IPlugin.ParseText) receives GAME text only. Genie client-side output never reaches it: #echo, #config, #highlight, #reload and script output all come back silent on 127.0.0.1:7416. Consequence: every # command sent through tools/genie.mjs is fire-and-forget and success is indistinguishable from failure. Verify a Genie config change by reading the .cfg file back, never by sending #reload and moving on. The check needs Genie running with the plugin loaded; it prints the probe line and nothing else, and if the probe string ever comes BACK the trap is fixed.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 17:49:24','2026-08-26 17:49:54','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/dr-companion && node tools/genie.mjs send "#echo ZQ-PROBE-7731" 4 | grep ZQ-PROBE-7731');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(78,'trap','genie-autolog-off-means-no-logs','C:\Genie4\Config\settings.cfg has #config {autolog} {False} on a fresh install, so C:\Genie4\Logs is EMPTY. Zero log files reads as "no errors were logged" when it actually means nothing was ever written. Check the autolog setting before concluding anything from an empty Logs directory.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 17:49:24','2026-08-26 17:49:54','grep -i autolog /c/Genie4/Config/settings.cfg');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(79,'trap','visual-rig-scene-activity-is-machine-wide','The "what the agent was doing" block in visual-rig scene output is machine-wide, not the focused session. With several Claude sessions running it interleaves all of their tool calls and carries NO field naming which session ran each one. Reading it as one session log led to messaging a peer to stop driving a game client it had never touched. Adjacency in a shared log is not attribution. The check greps a real scene for a session/agent identifier column: it finds none, which is the point.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 17:49:24','2026-08-26 17:49:54','visual-rig scene $(visual-rig clips --json | head -1) | sed -n "/what the agent was doing/,/^$/p" | grep -iE "session|agent id|pid" || echo "no actor field - trap still stands"');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(80,'trap','gemstone-wording-in-dragonrealms-configs','GemStone IV and DragonRealms are different games from the same company (Simutronics). Lich was built by the community for one and ported to the other, so a single toolchain and a single config culture span both, and the other game vocabulary leaks into DragonRealms configs where it fires on nothing. Seen TWICE in one file, so treat it as the default suspicion rather than a one-off: (1) the mindstate ladder - GemStone clear/muddled/numbed/saturated vs DragonRealms clear/dabbling/perusing/.../mind lock; (2) wound severity - a bare "severe" was the only one of DragonRealms thirteen levels present. THE FIX IS AN INSTRUMENT, NOT CARE: Lich must parse this text to work, so Lich holds the authoritative lists, and the DIRECTORY says which game. lib/dragonrealms/ is DragonRealms (drinfomon/drvariables.rb DR_LEARNING_RATES, commons/common-healing-data.rb WOUND_SEVERITY, LODGED_SEVERITY, PARASITES_REGEX, and regex constants whose comments carry worked examples of the real game lines). lib/constants.rb is the other game. Diff any DragonRealms word list BOTH ways against the lib/dragonrealms table before trusting it.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 17:58:20','2026-08-26 23:54:09','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/dr-genie-settings && node validate.mjs');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(81,'tool','magi-book-quality-tools','magi-reader-engine has a second gate beside validate.js: src/lib/book/quality.js asks whether a book can be BEATEN, not whether it parses. Tools around it: quality-report.mjs (npm run book:quality) scores every book worst-first; debias.mjs permutes options to even out answer position without touching text; verify-debias.mjs proves the permutation kept every answer''s exact string; length-tell.mjs shows per-question how much a distractor needs to stop the answer being longest; patch-options.mjs applies option rewrites but refuses any edit whose expected text has moved; show-questions.mjs prints options with lengths. All three books scored 100 on 27 Aug 2026 (were 76, 84, 58). The gate still scores a deliberately wrecked book 0, verified.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:01:46','2026-08-26 18:01:46','cd magi-app && npm run book:quality   -- expect three books, all score 100');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(82,'trap','magi-engine-pushes-master-to-main','magi-reader-engine''s local branch is master and its remote branch is main, so a bare ''git push'' is rejected with a message about branch.autoSetupMerge that does not say the branch names differ. Use: git push origin master:main. Then confirm by comparing git rev-parse HEAD against git ls-remote origin main, because the rejection is easy to read as success.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:01:47','2026-08-26 18:01:47','git -C <magi-app> rev-parse HEAD  and  git ls-remote origin main | cut -f1  -- equal means landed');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(83,'trap','magi-itch-serial-test-flakes-under-load','e2e/itch.spec.js''s @serial tests time out ONLY inside the full verify:full chain, never alone. MEASURED 27 Aug 2026 across five blocked pushes: --project=desktop alone passes in 3.6-3.7s against BOTH a two-book dist (1,256 files) and a one-book dist, so neither the shelf size nor the build is the cause. Inside verify:full it times out at 90s, and WHICH test fails moves between runs (the cross-origin iframe on desktop, then the third-party storage one on phone) -- a real regression fails the same test every time. Playwright''s own error-context.md snapshot shows the app rendering correctly at the moment of the timeout, and the built app drives fine in a browser (scene renders, 1 of 318, first plate decoded at 1024px). Cause is machine contention: 11 node and 14 chrome processes from parallel Claude sessions while the chain stands up two HTTP servers and four browser projects. DO NOT reach for --no-verify; re-run when the machine is quiet, and read the error-context snapshot before believing a failure.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:01:47','2026-08-27 03:19:27','cd magi-app && npx playwright test --grep @serial --workers=1 --project=desktop   -- passes in ~4s means the code is fine and the chain is starved');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(84,'trap','claude-dir-holds-session-keys','C:\Users\Admin\.claude\sessions\ contains *.key files (nine on 27 Aug 2026), so NEVER run git init plus git add -A in that directory: it commits credentials. It is also 333 MB, 331 MB of which is session transcripts under projects/. The hand-written part is about 150 KB. dev/claude-config versions that part by ALLOWLIST rather than gitignore, because a denylist protects you until someone adds a file nobody thought of, while an allowlist fails by missing something instead of by leaking it.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:06:41','2026-08-26 18:06:41','ls C:/Users/Admin/.claude/sessions/*.key | wc -l   -- nonzero means the hazard is live');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(85,'trap','claude-dir-holds-credentials','C:/Users/Admin/.claude must NEVER be made a git repository directly. .claude/sessions/ holds nine *.key files, and the directory is 334 MB of which 331 MB is session transcripts under projects/. A git init there is one ''git add -A'' from committing credentials. .gitignore is the wrong instrument because a denylist fails by leaking whatever nobody thought of. Copy by ALLOWLIST into dev/claude-config instead: CLAUDE.md, settings.json, the xref checkers, projects/*/memory/*.md. An allowlist fails by missing a file, which is the safe direction.','verified','verified 2026-08-27; I had advised the naive git init and was wrong','2026-08-26 18:08:40','2026-08-26 18:08:40','find C:/Users/Admin/.claude -name ''*.key'' | wc -l   # expect 9, not 0');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(86,'trap','autocrlf-silently-rewrites-a-backup','core.autocrlf is TRUE globally on this machine, so git stores LF and restores CRLF. For a repo whose purpose is fidelity that is corruption: dev/claude-config restored 32 of 33 memory notes with different bytes than the originals, because those notes are LF. CLAUDE.md is already CRLF, so it round-tripped perfectly and made the backup look sound -- the file most likely to be checked was the one file that could not reveal the bug. Fix: a .gitattributes containing ''* -text'' so nothing is translated, then re-add every file so the stored blobs are raw. Proved in an isolated repo: without .gitattributes an LF file DIFFERS after clone while a CRLF file is identical; with ''* -text'' both are identical. GENERAL FORM: a backup nobody has restored from is not a backup, and comparing only the file you happen to open can confirm the wrong thing.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:13:14','2026-08-26 18:13:14','cd C:/Users/Admin/dev/claude-config && python test_snapshot.py   -- the round-trip case clones and compares every file');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(87,'trap','backup-never-restored-is-not-a-backup','Every check on a new backup asks whether something bad got IN. The only question that matters is whether what got in comes back OUT unchanged. dev/claude-config passed five separate audits (gitleaks, two shape scans, two filename audits) and still restored 32 of 33 memory notes with different bytes: core.autocrlf=true globally, git stored LF and restored CRLF. Worse, CLAUDE.md is one of only 3 CRLF files among 37, so the single file anyone would spot-check was incapable of revealing the defect. Fix is ''* -text'' in .gitattributes plus a re-add. Round-trip means clone to a FRESH directory and compare bytes; cloning at HEAD~1 inside an existing checkout does not re-normalise and shows a false pass.','verified','clone-and-compare, 37/37 identical after fix; found by Magi Reader','2026-08-26 18:15:52','2026-08-26 18:15:52','git clone -q C:/Users/Admin/dev/claude-config /tmp/rt && diff -r --brief /tmp/rt C:/Users/Admin/.claude');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(88,'project','local-only-repos-sweep','Sweep of every repo under dev/ on 2026-08-27 asking ''ls-remote first, then count''. Three lack an off-machine copy: magi-reader (remote DELETED, 743 media files, 27.5 MB), claude-config (no remote by design, awaiting Dan), sirindhorn-m1-test (no remote, 10 commits, 41 files, 36 MB, ACTIVELY committed to 14 minutes before the sweep), world-aflame-unity (no remote, 1 commit, 20 files, 278 KB, the C# port of 150 card effects, superseded by world-aflame-godot). Everything else has a live remote and ahead=0. The ''dirty'' counts in gf-art (70), longnight (11) and others are pending DELETIONS whose content is safe in pushed history, not unbacked-up work.','verified','ls-remote --exit-code per repo, not rev-list','2026-08-26 18:15:52','2026-08-26 18:15:52','cd C:/Users/Admin/dev && for d in */; do git -C $d ls-remote --exit-code origin >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo $d; done');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(89,'trap','gitleaks-hook-passes-when-binary-missing','The pre-commit hook in these repos begins: GITLEAKS=<winget path>; [ -x "$GITLEAKS" ] || exit 0. If that binary is ever moved or removed -- a winget update relocating the Packages folder, or a cleanup pass -- EVERY commit then passes the secret scan silently, with no message and exit 0. A security gate that reports success by not running. Verified 27 Aug 2026: the binary is present (gitleaks 8.30.1) so the gate is live TODAY, but the failure mode is one uninstall away and would be invisible. Fix is one line: make the missing-binary branch print and exit 1 instead of exit 0, so it fails closed. That is Dan''s call because it would block commits until the path is repaired.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:20:52','2026-08-26 18:20:52','ls -x "C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Microsoft/WinGet/Packages/Gitleaks.Gitleaks_Microsoft.Winget.Source_8wekyb3d8bbwe/gitleaks.exe"  -- missing means the hook is silently passing everything');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(90,'tool','gitleaks-actually-fires','MEASURED 27 Aug 2026, because two sessions had been quoting ''no leaks found'' without either having seen it find anything. It works. Blocked: a realistic ghp_ PAT, a Slack xoxb token, an sk-proj OpenAI key, a full-length RSA private key, and a non-example AWS key pair. Allowed through: ghp_ followed by 36 identical characters (low entropy, correctly ignored), AWS''s own PUBLISHED example keys AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE and wJalrXUtnFEMI... (deliberately allowlisted), and a 20-character truncated private key body. All four passes were weak canaries, not defects. RESIDUAL CAVEAT, which is CLAUDE.md section 7 demonstrated fresh: a file literally named creds.txt containing a low-entropy token committed clean, so gitleaks is a vendor-pattern-and-entropy matcher and still not a substitute for checking by filename and shape.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:20:52','2026-08-26 18:20:52','see gltest.sh method: commit a realistic ghp_ token in a scratch repo carrying the hook; it must be blocked');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(91,'trap','gitleaks-hook-failed-open','The global pre-commit hook ended its lookup with ''[ -x $GITLEAKS ] || exit 0'', so if the winget path ever moved every commit in every repo passed the secret scan silently, no output, exit 0. DEMONSTRATED: same hook, same AWS key pair; binary present blocks the commit, path broken commits it clean and prints nothing. Binary is present today (8.30.1) and all 23 repos under dev/ carry the hook, so the gate is live -- the failure is one uninstall away and invisible. HARDENED TEMPLATE 27 Aug 2026: winget path, then PATH fallback, then block loudly naming the reason. A moved install keeps working; a real absence stops the commit instead of waving it through. Template only: the 23 existing repos still carry the old copy because init.templateDir applies at init/clone, and rolling it out mid-session would change commit behaviour under five live sessions.','verified','found by Magi Reader; independently demonstrated both directions','2026-08-26 18:23:45','2026-08-26 18:23:45','grep -c ''could not be found'' C:/Users/Admin/.git-templates/hooks/pre-commit   # expect 1');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(92,'trap','magi-app-has-no-secret-scanning','All 23 repos under dev/ carry a gitleaks pre-commit hook. magi-reader-engine does NOT, and it is the repo that gets published. It lives at Downloads/Legacy.../magi-app, outside dev/, so a sweep whose denominator is dev/ reports 23 of 23 clean and misses it entirely. It uses husky with core.hooksPath=.husky/_ and its pre-commit is ''npx lint-staged''; nothing in .husky or package.json mentions gitleaks. Downloads/testgrader IS scanned, so the gap is specific rather than a Downloads problem. Verified 27 Aug 2026 by reading the hook and by committing a real-shaped AWS key pair into a scratch clone, which succeeded. THE GENERAL POINT: when auditing coverage, the denominator must be every repo on the machine, not every repo in the folder where repos are supposed to live.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:27:01','2026-08-26 18:27:01','grep -rl gitleaks ''<magi-app>/.husky'' ''<magi-app>/package.json''  -- no output means no secret scanning');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(93,'trap','a-weak-canary-produces-a-FALSE-DEFECT','The mirror of the zero rule, and it bites in the opposite direction. Testing gitleaks, my first canary was ''ghp_'' plus 36 identical characters. It committed clean and I nearly reported the security tool broken. The canary was the problem: low entropy, correctly ignored. Two further passes were AWS''s own PUBLISHED example keys, which gitleaks deliberately allowlists. Four apparent failures, zero real ones. So: an instrument that fails your test may be right and your test may be wrong, and ''the security tool is broken'' is a finding people act on quickly. Make the canary realistic, and when a tool disagrees with your test, suspect the test first.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:27:01','2026-08-26 18:27:01',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(94,'trap','repo-audit-denominator-is-the-machine','A coverage audit''s denominator must be every repo on the MACHINE, not every repo in the folder where repos are supposed to live. Two sessions independently reported ''23 of 23 repos have the gitleaks hook'' and both counted the same wrong set: there are 26. The three outside dev/ are magi-app (published as magi-reader-engine, uses husky with per-repo core.hooksPath=.husky/_ and NO gitleaks), Downloads/testgrader (scanned, fine), and source/repos/demo_selfhelp (empty, 0 commits, remote belongs to xM4sterMindx not Dan). SECOND HALF: checking ''git config --global core.hooksPath'' is not enough -- a PER-REPO core.hooksPath silently redirects hooks away from .git/hooks, which is exactly how magi-app escaped. Query it per repo, without --global.','verified','find for .git across the profile, 2026-08-27; magi-app gap found by Magi Reader','2026-08-26 18:29:11','2026-08-26 18:29:11','cd C:/Users/Admin && find . -name node_modules -prune -o -type d -name .git -print | wc -l   # expect 26, not 23');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(95,'project','magi-app-scanned-clean','magi-app (Downloads/Legacy.../magi-app, published as dancockrell/magi-reader-engine) had NO secret scanning: husky pre-commit runs only ''npx lint-staged''. Audited 2026-08-27 and it is CLEAN: gitleaks over 56 commits / 30.43 MB found no leaks; 166 tracked files carry no credential-shaped names, and none was ever added and later deleted. Canaries proved both instruments fire. The gate is still absent -- the fix is adding gitleaks to .husky/pre-commit, left to the Magi Reader session since they are committing to it live.','verified','gitleaks via a NATIVE Windows path; the MSYS /c/ form fails FTL and scans nothing','2026-08-26 18:29:11','2026-08-26 18:29:11',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(97,'trap','husky-runs-hooks-with-sh-e','husky v9''s wrapper (.husky/_/h) invokes hooks as `sh -e "$s"`, so ANY command returning non-zero kills the hook on that line. This silently removes error reporting from hooks that look correct: `scan=$(gitleaks protect --staged)` exits the script the instant gitleaks finds something, BEFORE the exit code is read and before any message prints, so the caller sees only ''husky - pre-commit script failed (code 1)''. It blocks correctly and explains nothing, which reads as output suppression rather than an early exit and cost about an hour to diagnose. Hit TWICE in one file: the same trap sat on the `command -v` fallback assignment. FIX: put the command in an `if` condition (exempt from -e) or append `|| true`. Note also that a hook''s messages should go to STDERR; stdout from a hook is not reliably shown.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 18:37:37','2026-08-26 18:37:37','grep -n ''sh -e'' <repo>/.husky/_/h   -- present means every non-zero line is fatal');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(98,'trap','no-itch-game-resolves-for-this-key','27 Aug 2026: butler cannot reach ANY itch game for this account. The key authenticates and the user resolves -- a bogus account gives ''invalid target (bad user)'' while dancockrell/<anything> gives ''invalid game'', which is a different error -- but every slug tried fails, INCLUDING dancockrell/ghost-front, which is hard-coded in the working push script at dev/gf-tools/tools/push.sh and therefore existed. dancockrell.itch.io 302-redirects to itch.io/profile/dancockrell with no projects listed, which is what itch does when a user has no game pages. So either the itch projects were deleted, or ~/.config/itch/butler_creds (42 bytes, modified 21 Aug) belongs to a different account than the games did. Butler CANNOT create a game and has no command to list games -- every subcommand needs a target you already know -- so this cannot be resolved from the CLI. The project page has to be created or identified in the itch.io web UI first. Never open or print butler_creds.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 23:59:16','2026-08-26 23:59:16','butler status dancockrell/ghost-front   -- ''invalid game'' means no reachable project; a channel listing means it is fixed');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(99,'tool','magi-reader-release-artifacts','npm run release in magi-app produces two zips in release/, named from package.json version. At 0.8.0: magi-reader-0.8.0-reader.zip (748 files, 29.3 MB) and magi-reader-0.8.0-legacy.zip (745 files, 29.5 MB). Both verified with butler auditzip (''Everything checks out''), both carry index.html at the archive root, and both sit under itch''s 1000-file limit, which is the constraint that shaped the pack format. release/ is gitignored; the git tag is what is durable. NOTE: npm run release chains verify:full first, which re-runs the whole e2e suite and fails intermittently on the @serial itch test under load; the build steps can be run directly when HEAD has already passed the chain at push time.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-26 23:59:16','2026-08-26 23:59:16','cd magi-app && ls -la release/*.zip && butler auditzip release/magi-reader-*-reader.zip');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(100,'trap','iso-date-only-parses-as-utc','An ISO date-only string parses as MIDNIGHT UTC (spec), but Date.now() is an instant, so subtracting them on a machine east of UTC gives a NEGATIVE age for something added today. Math.floor turns -0.09 days into -1, and any "age >= threshold" test then silently never fires. Cost: a staleness check in dr-genie-settings that could not fire at all, while printing "-1 days" on screen under a summary that said "all passed". Fix: take BOTH sides at UTC midnight - Date.UTC(now.getUTCFullYear(), now.getUTCMonth(), now.getUTCDate()) minus Date.parse(dateOnly) - use Math.round, and make a negative age a hard failure rather than clamping it, since a future date is a typo that would hide the entry from ageing for as long as it stayed wrong. This machine is east of UTC, so the bug reproduces here and would be invisible in a US timezone.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:02:01','2026-08-27 00:02:01','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/dr-genie-settings && DR_STALE_DAYS=0 node validate.mjs | tail -1');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(101,'reference','itch-target-gift-of-the-magi','The itch.io target for Magi Reader is dancockrell/the-gift-of-the-magi, channel html. Pushed 0.8.0 on 27 Aug 2026: build #1919082, upload #18973417, 29.26 MiB. The slug was expensive to find because the project is a DRAFT -- drafts are 404 to anonymous fetch and absent from the public profile, and butler has no command to list games, so every subcommand needs a slug you already know. Probe with butler status dancockrell/<slug>: ''invalid game'' means wrong slug, ''invalid target (bad user)'' means wrong account, and ''No channel found'' means the project exists and is empty. Push with: butler push release/magi-reader-<v>-reader.zip dancockrell/the-gift-of-the-magi:html --userversion <v>','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:09:23','2026-08-27 00:09:23','butler status dancockrell/the-gift-of-the-magi   -- a channel table means the target is live');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(102,'trap','butler-cannot-create-an-itch-project','butler creates CHANNELS, never PROJECTS. A channel comes into existence as a side effect of a successful push; the push itself fails first if no project exists, with ''creating build on remote server: itch.io API error (400): /wharf/builds: invalid game''. There is no butler command to make a game and none to list games. The project page must be created at itch.io/game/new in the web UI, with Kind of project set to HTML for it to be playable in a browser rather than a download. Also note butler push --dry-run does NOT contact the API at all -- it only lists local files, so it cannot be used to test whether a target resolves. Use butler status for that.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:09:23','2026-08-27 00:09:23',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(103,'reference','itch-target-the-raven','The Raven''s itch project is dancockrell/the-raven-edgar-allen-poe -- note ALLEN, not Allan, which is a misspelling of Poe''s name carried in the slug and the page title. Zero channels as of 27 Aug 2026; NOT pushed, see [[raven-has-no-forward-build-tool]]. The Gift of the Magi is at dancockrell/the-gift-of-the-magi and IS pushed at 0.8.0. Both projects are RESTRICTED, which is itch''s default for a new project and which Dan opens manually.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:10:59','2026-08-27 00:10:59','butler status dancockrell/the-raven-edgar-allen-poe');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(104,'trap','raven-has-no-forward-build-tool','The Raven repo''s pipeline runs only BACKWARDS: build/the-raven.html -> extract-book.mjs -> book/book.json -> fix-glossary.mjs -> pack/book.json. Nothing goes pack -> build; both tools in tools/ only READ the html. So edits to pack/book.json cannot be shipped, because the only distributable artifact is build/the-raven.html, dated 25 Aug and never regenerated. PROVEN 27 Aug 2026: after fixing the book''s questions, build/the-raven.html still contains ''Morning will never come'' and ''holy, made a saint'' (the old text) while pack/book.json contains ''Dawn is still a great many hours away'' and ''holy and blessed''. Pushing that build to itch would silently ship back the 50% answer-position bias, the 82% longest-option tell, the circular gloss and the absolute distractors -- undoing the fixes invisibly, because the artifact looks current. The magi engine cannot ship it either: it loads books from src/books/ and the raven lives in its own pack repo, with the bring-your-own-pack contract still unbuilt.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:10:59','2026-08-27 00:10:59','grep -c ''Morning will never come'' <raven>/build/the-raven.html  -- 1 means the build is still stale');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(105,'tool','raven-forward-build-tool','BUILT 27 Aug 2026, closing the gap in [[raven-has-no-forward-build-tool]] which is now RESOLVED. tools/build-reader.mjs in the raven repo writes pack/book.json back INTO build/the-raven.html: it replaces the TEACHING literal wholesale and swaps changed gloss definitions individually. Refuses if the pack lacks a unit the build has, if a gloss string is not unique in the file, if the size moves by more than the edit explains, or if the rewritten literal does not read back as the pack. tools/lib-literal.mjs finds a balanced `var NAME = {...}` span (lifted from the engine''s extract-book.mjs; a regex cannot do it because the stanzas are full of braces). Art and audio are data URIs elsewhere and are never touched. Run: node tools/build-reader.mjs [--write]','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:18:28','2026-08-27 00:18:28','cd <raven> && node tools/build-reader.mjs   -- ''The build already matches the pack'' means they are in sync');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(106,'trap','raven-pack-is-missing-its-act-reviews','pack/book.json in the raven repo has NO recaps: 28 mc questions across 14 units and zero act reviews, where the shipped build has five (s3, s6, s8, s10, s12). They live in a separate `var RECAPS = {...}` literal in the HTML, and the engine''s extract-book.mjs folds them into teaching[id].recap -- a fold that was ADDED after this pack was generated, so the pack predates it. Consequence: a pack-driven reader loses all five act reviews, exactly the way four magi act reviews once shipped unasked. The shipped single-file build is unaffected, because RECAPS is deliberately untouched by tools/build-reader.mjs. Fix is to regenerate the pack from the current build with the current extractor, which was not done on 27 Aug to avoid mixing it into the release.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 00:18:28','2026-08-27 00:18:28','node -e "const b=require(''<raven>/pack/book.json'');console.log(Object.values(b.teaching).filter(t=>t.recap).length)"   -- 0 means still missing, 5 means fixed');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(108,'trap','cargo-clean-p-is-not-recoverable','''cargo clean -p <crate>'' deletes cached build-script OUTPUT which may be unregeneratable if the linker is broken. Ran on web_atoms to clear an apparently stale artifact; the build script then could not be relinked (see trap msvc-x64-crt-libs-missing) so ''cargo check'' in dr-companion/src-tauri went from passing to failing and STAYED there. The cached artifact was the only reason check worked at all (see trap cargo-check-does-not-link). Before cleaning a dependency cache, confirm it can be rebuilt: the clean is a deletion of a derived artefact and the loss is silent until the next build. Found by DR Companion 27 Aug 2026; cross-reference repointed after the msvc rows were merged.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 01:34:15','2026-08-27 04:35:17','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/quartermaster && cmd //c build.cmd build > /dev/null 2>&1 && echo ''linker OK - a cargo clean -p would be recoverable now'' || echo ''linker BROKEN - do NOT cargo clean -p anything''');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(109,'reference','how-to-add-a-book-to-magi-reader','READ docs/ADDING-A-BOOK.md in magi-app BEFORE porting a title. The shape: the repository is the READER, a book is a PACK it is handed, and one store release is the reader plus EXACTLY ONE pack. Seven steps: pack folder (book.json, index.js, pack.test.js) / check-book.mjs / index.js declares media and imports JSON with `with { type: ''json'' }` / register in src/books/index.js ALL / add the source to ROOTS in copy-assets.mjs and run npm run assets / build with `node tools/pack-book.mjs <id>` NOT npm run build / push one book to one itch page. Enforced by src/books/registry.test.js. npm run book:pack <id> is the release build.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 02:36:43','2026-08-27 02:36:43','cd magi-app && npx vitest run src/books/registry.test.js   -- fails if a registered book is not a proper pack');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(110,'feedback','an-old-build-is-not-a-port','Dan, 27 Aug 2026, on shipping build/the-raven.html to itch: ''that''s an old html build, depreciated... needs porting properly'' and ''you are building bad code if it isn''t built to the same standard''. WHY IT MATTERS: the old single-file reader RAN, so it looked finished. Running is not the bar. A previous generation of the application with its content inlined is not a book on the current engine, and shipping it silently ships the old app. THE STANDARD IS THE OTHER BOOK: whatever magi has, the new title has too -- a pack.test.js of the same rigour, media brought in by the same reproducible tool, the same release path. Half a port that works on this machine is the failure mode, because nothing errors: missing media is silence and a hole in the page.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 02:36:43','2026-08-27 02:36:43',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(111,'tool','visual-rig-verified','github.com/dancockrell/desktop-vision-rig, MIT. Claims verified 2026-08-27 rather than relayed: 81 test functions (exactly as claimed), MIT confirmed, remote contains local HEAD. doctor reports what it DOES not what it could -- ''watcher: polling (watchdog installed, not yet used)'' -- which is the section 9 defect it was previously criticised for, now fixed. ''running'' and ''duplicates'' both work; duplicates is well-judged (''Listed, not accused''). Run from its own venv: dev/visual-rig/.venv/Scripts/visual-rig.exe. NOTE: its port-holder output is ACCURATE -- I nearly filed a false bug because Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort N -State Listen returns fewer rows than netstat -ano for the same port.','verified','counted tests, ran doctor/running/duplicates, cross-checked with netstat','2026-08-27 03:17:39','2026-08-27 03:17:39','C:/Users/Admin/dev/visual-rig/.venv/Scripts/visual-rig.exe doctor');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(112,'trap','get-nettcpconnection-undercounts-listeners','Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort N -State Listen under-reports. On port 5200 it returned 2 listeners where ''netstat -ano'' showed 4 rows across 3 distinct PIDs, and a per-process query of the same cmdlet agreed with netstat. Two queries of ONE API disagreeing is the signal to reach for a different instrument, not to pick the answer you like. This nearly produced a false bug report against a working tool -- the mirror of a weak canary declaring a good scanner broken.','verified','port 5200, three python -m http.server processes, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 03:17:39','2026-08-27 03:17:39','netstat -ano | grep '':5200 '' | grep -c LISTENING   # compare against the cmdlet');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(113,'trap','msys-paths-break-windows-tools','Anything that is not an MSYS program cannot resolve /c/Users/... paths, and the failure often LOOKS like a clean result. Three instances in one night: gitleaks.exe printed ''FTL CreateFile ... cannot find the path'' and scanned 0 bytes where the native path scanned 30.43 MB; Python''s sqlite3.connect raised ''unable to open database file''; and in a test harness that error scrolled past and the run printed ''unchanged - nothing to do'', which reads exactly like a pass. Pass C:/ or C:\ form to any .exe or to Python, and read the work-done line (bytes scanned, rows counted) rather than the verdict.','verified','gitleaks 0 vs 30.43MB; sqlite3 OperationalError; guard test that silently did nothing','2026-08-27 03:28:10','2026-08-27 03:28:10','python -c "import sqlite3;sqlite3.connect(r''/c/Users/Admin/dev/memory-db/memory.db'').execute(''select 1'')"   # must RAISE');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(114,'trap','guard-that-runs-after-the-write','I added a collapse guard to backup.py and placed it AFTER the two write_text calls it was meant to protect. The guard then read the file it had just overwritten, so previous_rows always equalled rows and the condition could never be true. A check that cannot fail, written into the tool built to catch checks that cannot fail, on the night spent cataloguing them. Order matters as much as logic: a guard must read the world as it was BEFORE the action it guards. Demonstrated after fixing -- wiped 102 of 107 facts, backup refused with exit 1 and wrote nothing, --force overrode deliberately.','verified','self-inflicted 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 03:28:11','2026-08-27 03:28:11','python C:/Users/Admin/dev/memory-db/test_roundtrip.py   # and see backup.py''s REFUSING path');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(115,'trap','vs-install-damaged-vcvars-silent','RESOLVED 27 Aug 2026 by appending ''C:/Program Files (x86)/Microsoft Visual Studio/Installer'' to the USER PATH. The mechanism is still worth knowing because it is a perfect silent failure: vcvars64.bat invokes vswhere.exe by BARE NAME, so if the VS Installer directory is not on PATH it finds nothing, prints ''[vcvarsall.bat] Environment initialized for: x64'', sets NOTHING, and EXITS 0. A success banner and a zero exit code over an empty environment. The VS repair did NOT fix this - it is a PATH problem, not corruption. NEVER read vcvars'' exit code; test whether LIB is actually defined afterwards. Verified: vcvars now sets LIB standalone in a fresh shell.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 03:58:34','2026-08-27 04:43:30','cmd //c ''call "C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvars64.bat" >nul 2>&1 & if defined LIB (echo LIB IS SET) else (echo LIB UNSET - vcvars is silently doing nothing)''');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(116,'trap','msvc-x64-crt-libs-missing','RESOLVED 27 Aug 2026 by a Visual Studio Installer repair - kept as a record because the failure was silent and may recur. WAS: MSVC 14.40.33807 lib/x64 missing vcruntime.lib, oldnames.lib and legacy_stdio_definitions.lib (the dynamic /MD CRT import libs Rust''s msvc target uses), while lib/onecore/x64 had all three. Symptom LNK1104 then LNK1181. Verified fixed: clean ''cargo build --release'' and 35 tests pass with NO crt-static and NO onecore fallback. FIX: vs_installer/setup.exe repair --installPath "<path>" --passive --norestart. NOTE the quotes: an unquoted path with spaces parses as ''C:\Program'' and the installer exits 1 having done nothing. IF IT RECURS: append lib/onecore/x64 to LIB *LAST* (dr-companion linked a full Tauri binary that way, no crt-static needed); do NOT copy onecore/store libs into lib/x64.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 03:58:34','2026-08-27 04:43:30','for f in vcruntime.lib oldnames.lib legacy_stdio_definitions.lib; do test -f ''/c/Program Files/Microsoft Visual Studio/2022/Community/VC/Tools/MSVC/14.40.33807/lib/x64/''$f && echo "x64/$f PRESENT" || echo "x64/$f MISSING - regression, repair VS"; done');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(117,'trap','cargo-not-on-git-bash-path','cargo and rustc live at C:/Users/Admin/.cargo/bin but are NOT on the Git Bash PATH, so a bare-name check reports Rust missing when it is installed. export PATH=/c/Users/Admin/.cargo/bin:$PATH first. Same shape as node (C:/Program Files/nodejs) and gh (C:/Program Files/GitHub CLI).','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 03:58:34','2026-08-27 03:58:53','which cargo || ls /c/Users/Admin/.cargo/bin/cargo.exe');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(118,'trap','cache-reload-does-not-bypass-a-service-worker','fetch(url, {cache: ''reload''}) does NOT get past a service worker. `cache` is an HTTP-cache directive; the worker''s fetch handler intercepts the request regardless, and caches.match() inside it ignores the mode entirely, so a cache-first worker answers both the plain fetch and the ''fresh'' one from the same cached response. MEASURED 27 Aug 2026 against a cache-first fixture with the file on disk changed underneath a running page: plain -> VERSION ONE, {cache:''reload''} -> VERSION ONE, same URL with ?bust=... -> VERSION TWO. To reach the network past a worker, append a query the worker has never cached so it misses caches.match. To reload a page past every cache, use CDP Page.reload with ignoreCache: true. This broke visual-rig''s staleness check, which reported ''matched a fresh fetch'' about a page demonstrably running replaced code.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 04:00:52','2026-08-27 04:00:52','cd C:/Users/Admin/dev/visual-rig && .venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest tests/ -q -k staleness_bypasses');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(119,'trap','f5-through-cdp-does-not-reload','Sending F5 via CDP Input.dispatchKeyEvent does NOT reload a page. The key is delivered to the DOCUMENT''s handlers; reload is browser chrome. Measured: after dispatching F5 the page''s performance.now() kept climbing and the DOM was untouched, while the CLI reported ''pressed: F5'' -- a command that succeeds and does nothing. Use CDP Page.reload (with ignoreCache: true to get past a service worker). Function keys are still worth having in a key table because a page may bind them; they are just not a reload.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 04:00:52','2026-08-27 04:00:52',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(120,'tool','openclaw-gateway-loopback','OpenClaw 2026.7.1-2 Gateway, node.exe on 127.0.0.1:18789, started by scheduled task ''OpenClaw Gateway'' (LogonTrigger, State Ready). TESTED 2026-08-27, and the two halves of its stated boundary have DIFFERENT standing. (1) Loopback-only: VERIFIED twice - netstat shows no 0.0.0.0 or [::] listener, and Test-NetConnection to this machine''s LAN address 192.168.1.14:18789 returns False. That is the boundary that actually protects the machine and it holds. (2) Token auth: UNCHECKED, not verified. GET / returns 200 with the dashboard HTML and no token, /health returns 200 {ok:true}, and eight guessed /api/* paths returned 404 - which cannot distinguish ''auth rejected me'' from ''those routes do not exist''. Extracting real paths from the 369 KB JS bundle found none, so the extraction failed too. Root page leaks no token-shaped strings. CLI is at AppData/Roaming/npm and NOT on the Git Bash PATH.','verified','netstat + Test-NetConnection + unauthenticated HTTP probes, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 04:32:22','2026-08-27 06:52:38','netstat -ano | grep '':18789 '' | grep LISTENING   # must show 127.0.0.1 only');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(122,'trap','npm-skips-postinstall-silently','npm 11.17 here does NOT run a package''s install scripts by default. A global install prints ''added N packages'', exits 0, and leaves an INCOMPLETE install; the only sign is ''npm warn allow-scripts N package has install scripts not yet covered by allowScripts'' buried in the output. Hit with @anthropic-ai/claude-code (postinstall node install.cjs) and 3 of OpenClaw''s deps. Fix: re-run with --allow-scripts=<package>. WHICH PACKAGES IT CAN BITE (tested by the Quick Grade session): only ones that still rely on a lifecycle script. Modern Playwright has NO postinstall - browsers come from an explicit ''npx playwright install'' - so it is immune and quickgrade was unaffected. So the one-command triage is ''npm ls <pkg> --json | grep scripts'' or ''npm view <pkg> scripts'': no postinstall means nothing to skip. Read the tail of a global npm install, never the exit code, and then run the binary.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 04:33:45','2026-08-27 05:03:23','PATH="/c/Program Files/nodejs:$PATH" npm config get allow-scripts; echo ''(unset/false = global installs skip postinstall scripts)''');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(123,'trap','cargo-check-does-not-link','''cargo check'' PASSES while ''cargo build'' and ''cargo test'' cannot link, because check never invokes the linker and reuses cached build-script output. So a machine with a broken MSVC linker looks healthy under check. Found by DR Companion 27 Aug 2026: dr-companion passed check for hours while being unable to build. Never accept ''cargo check'' as evidence that a toolchain works - it is the Rust instance of ''a check that cannot fail is not a check''. Use ''cargo build'' or ''cargo test'' to prove linking.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 04:35:02','2026-08-27 04:35:02','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/quartermaster && cmd //c build.cmd build > /dev/null 2>&1 && echo ''LINKING WORKS'' || echo ''LINK BROKEN (check would still have passed)''');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(124,'trap','crlf-rule-not-reproducible-today','CLAUDE.md rule 5 says cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only .cmd/.bat files. Measured 2026-08-27 on Windows 11 build 26200: LF-only and CRLF produced IDENTICAL output across six constructs - plain echo, a quoted call to a path with spaces, an if/else paren block, a for loop with a paren body, goto plus a label, and set with a spaced value. So the rule as stated does not reproduce here. DO NOT DELETE IT: the original failure was real and its symptom was a misleading Python-interpreter path error, so the trigger is probably a construct not covered above or an encoding/BOM issue, and failing to reproduce something is a claim about the test rather than about the world. CRLF costs one sed and the failure costs an hour, so keep writing CRLF; this row exists so nobody spends another hour re-deriving the measurement.','verified','six-construct LF vs CRLF comparison, cygpath-normalised invocation','2026-08-27 04:46:10','2026-08-27 04:46:10','C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Temp/... see value; recreate the six cases and diff LF vs CRLF output');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(125,'trap','backslash-halving-escapes-your-variable','Second-order form of bash-tool-eats-one-backslash and much nastier. Writing a Windows path as "$DIR\${name}.cmd" halves the backslash run to one, and that single backslash then ESCAPES the dollar of the very variable being expanded: the shell receives $DIR\.cmd, emits the literal text dollar-brace-name, and drops the separator. The result is a path that looks almost right in an error message and silently addresses a file that cannot exist. Cost several minutes of debugging a comparison whose two columns both said ''is not recognized'' while a hand-typed sanity case worked. Remedy: build Windows paths with cygpath -w "$PWD/name" and never place a backslash immediately before a variable expansion.','verified','LF/CRLF harness, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 04:46:10','2026-08-27 04:46:10',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(126,'trap','magi-reader-remote-deleted','URGENT, UNRESOLVED as of 27 Aug 2026. C:/Users/Admin/dev/magi-reader has a DELETED remote (github.com/dancockrell/magi-reader returns a hard 404 = deleted, not renamed; GitHub 301-redirects renames forever). git reports it healthy: ''status -sb'' prints ''## main...origin/main'', ''rev-list --count origin/main..HEAD'' says 0 unpushed, ''branch -vv'' shows [origin/main]. Only ''git ls-remote --exit-code origin'' disagrees (exit 128). 748 tracked files. AUDIO IS SAFE: 519 mp3s survive in dev/claude-agent/deliver/magi-itch-folder.zip, more than the 477 on disk. ART IS NOT: 174 .webp in magi-reader/art exist NOWHERE else on this machine, not in the itch zip (audio only), not in magi-reader-engine (code only, 166 files, no media). DO NOT DELETE that directory. Fix is Dan''s call - the repo was probably deleted deliberately during the rename to magi-reader-engine.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 05:15:27','2026-08-27 05:15:27','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/magi-reader && git ls-remote --exit-code origin >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo ''REMOTE ALIVE - resolved'' || echo ''STILL DEAD - 174 art files backed up nowhere''');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(127,'project','world-aflame-lore-authority','Project 42 lore/art/sound is owned by ONE dedicated loremaster thread (assigned by Dan 27 Aug 2026: ''listen to the project 42 loremaster, they are in charge. if they are wrong I will fix them''). Scope covers the whole Project 42 universe including World Aflame and The Long Night. NOT the session named ''Project 42'' - that owns mechanics/engine/ledger/balance and has declined lore. Authority doc: world-aflame-godot/docs/LORE-BIBLE.md, committed. Reach the loremaster via ListAgents + SendMessage. Memory files are pointers only, never copies - the lore was lost twice because it lived only in session context.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 05:40:18','2026-08-27 06:19:45','gh api repos/dancockrell/world-aflame-godot/contents/docs/LORE-BIBLE.md --jq .size');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(128,'trap','cargo-registry-src-files-deleted','Two .rs files were deleted from an EXTRACTED crate in ~/.cargo/registry/src on 26 Aug 2026 at 16:06, leaving the rest of the crate alone: serde_core-1.0.229/src/de/mod.rs and impls.rs went, src/ser/ stayed intact at its original Aug 25 timestamp. The .crate archive in registry/cache was untouched and still contains all four files, so nothing needs re-downloading - restore the missing files from the archive with tar, or delete the extracted directory and let cargo re-extract. ''cargo clean -p <crate>'' does NOT help: it clears build artifacts, not extracted source. Suspect antivirus quarantine or a disk-cleanup pass; whatever did it will do it again, and the next crate it hits may fail less obviously than a compile error. CRITICAL DIAGNOSTIC: a machine with this damage can still build green from a warm target dir, because the prebuilt rlib means cargo never re-reads the source. Only a fresh CARGO_TARGET_DIR exposes it. I wrongly told another session their failure was local because my cached build passed.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 05:51:02','2026-08-27 05:51:02','tar -tzf ~/.cargo/registry/cache/index.crates.io-*/serde_core-1.0.229.crate | grep -c ''src/de/'' # 4 in the archive; compare: ls ~/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-*/serde_core-1.0.229/src/de/ | wc -l');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(129,'trap','transcript-path-is-not-scratchpad-path','A session summary cites the PRIOR conversation''s transcript as C:\Users\Admin\.claude\projects\<project>\<UUID>.jsonl. That UUID looks exactly like a scratchpad UUID but is NOT yours. Your scratchpad is named separately in your own system prompt. On 27 Aug 2026 a session took the transcript UUID as its scratchpad and wrote into ANOTHER LIVE SESSION''s working directory all afternoon; its own scratchpad sat empty. Failure is silent in both directions - you clobber nothing and the Write tool reports real success, so the success covers a narrower claim than the sentence it licenses. It also caused a false authorship claim against a peer, because a file in that directory looked like it must be yours. Check: your scratchpad path appears verbatim in your system prompt; list the directory before assuming a file in it is yours.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 05:56:16','2026-08-27 05:56:16',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(130,'trap','project-42-lore-owner','UPDATE 27 Aug 2026: the lore master''s session context has since CLOSED. Canon now lives in world-aflame-godot/docs/ as six-plus volumes (LORE-BIBLE.md, WORLD-TIMELINE.md, WORLD-CAMP-IRON-BELL.md, WORLD-HYAKKI-YAKO.md, WORLD-THE-SETTLED.md, WORLD-WERK-NACHTIGALL.md, ART-SPEC.md) rather than one file -- read those directly rather than assuming a session is still there to ask. A shared Discord channel now exists for cross-session lore questions so answers are not lost when a context closes again: see memory row project-42-discord-coordination. Original finding stands: the session named ''Project 42'' explicitly declined the lore role twice; the lore-owning session identified itself in Discord/commits as holding lore, art and sound.','reported',NULL,'2026-08-27 06:19:01','2026-08-27 08:57:58','ls C:/Users/Admin/dev/world-aflame-godot/docs/*.md | wc -l');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(131,'trap','gateway-is-shared-singleton-state','The OpenClaw Gateway on 127.0.0.1:18789 is shared singleton state across every session on this machine. Do NOT run ''openclaw onboard'' again and do not restart the gateway casually - every other session using it goes down with it. Same class as CLAUDE.md section 4, where launching a second client instance silently disconnected Dan''s live session twice. Say so before restarting. Reported by the Claude Claw session, which restarted it twice in one day and flagged that as two more than ideal.','reported','Claude Claw session','2026-08-27 06:52:38','2026-08-27 06:52:38','Get-ScheduledTask ''OpenClaw Gateway'' | Select State   # and check who else is attached before touching it');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(132,'trap','resolve-session-id-never-infer-it','Cross-session messages carry a PIPE id and a display NAME; neither is the session id SendMessage needs, and sessions rename themselves mid-run - one pipe appeared first as ''Claude scheduler'', later as ''Claude Claw''. I inferred an id from an earlier message on that pipe and delivered a security report to the wrong session. Call the list_sessions tool and match the CURRENT title before replying. No shell check exists by design: this is a rule about tool use, not a machine fact.','verified','misrouted an OpenClaw report, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 06:54:22','2026-08-27 09:43:25',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(133,'trap','openclaw-token-not-enforced-on-handshake','MEASURED 2026-08-27: the OpenClaw Gateway accepts a WebSocket upgrade on ws://127.0.0.1:18789 with NO x-openclaw-token header. Both the authorised control and the tokenless attempt returned HTTP 101 ACCEPTED, so the client is not broken - the handshake simply does not require a token. Config says gateway.auth.mode=token and a token is set, so auth is CONFIGURED but not ENFORCED at the handshake. SCOPE, precisely: this tests the upgrade only. Whether the JSON-RPC layer demands auth on the first message is a SEPARATE question and is UNTESTED - no RPC was sent deliberately. Practical exposure is bounded by the loopback bind (verified: Test-NetConnection to 192.168.1.14:18789 returns False), so only processes on this machine can reach it - but on a box running a dozen agent sessions that is not nothing. Note: findToken pulled a 48-char value while the owning session reported the gateway token as 21 chars, so the control may have used a different secret; this does not weaken the finding, since the decisive case sent NO token at all.','verified','node http upgrade probe with control, handshake only, nothing sent over the socket','2026-08-27 06:58:52','2026-08-27 06:58:52','node C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Temp/claude/C--Users-Admin-Downloads/a9593032-331b-4a8b-99d0-f5f35a1e0cf2/scratchpad/wsprobe.js');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(134,'tool','webview2-cdp-debugging','A Tauri app''s WebView2 opens a DevTools protocol port if it is started with the environment variable WEBVIEW2_ADDITIONAL_BROWSER_ARGUMENTS=--remote-debugging-port=9223. Verified on dr-companion 27 Aug 2026: the endpoint answers, Target.getTargets lists the app page, and Runtime.evaluate / Input.dispatchMouseEvent / Page.captureScreenshot all work against the real app - localStorage, the Tauri bridge and the live socket included. This is the only way to see a Tauri app; a browser pointed at the Vite dev server has isTauri() false and renders every empty branch perfectly, so it can only tell you the empty state has no bugs in it. Driver: dr-companion/tools/app-eyes.mjs (status|start|shot|text|eval|click|overflow), reusing attach() in tools/browser.mjs. Attach to a page target that already exists - creating one gives a blank page with none of the app in it. The tool refuses chrome-error://chromewebdata/, because an error page reports a perfectly clean layout and reads as a pass.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 06:58:54','2026-08-27 06:59:08','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/dr-companion && node tools/app-eyes.mjs start && node tools/app-eyes.mjs eval "location.href + '' roots='' + document.querySelectorAll(''#root'').length"');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(135,'trap','discord-4014-disallowed-intents','OpenClaw Discord channel fails with ''gateway websocket closed code=4014 reason=Disallowed intent(s)'' when the Discord app''s PRIVILEGED gateway intents are off. The token can be perfectly valid and the bot identity resolves (''Discord bot probe resolved @Open Claw - Project 42'') while the gateway connection still closes immediately - so ''configured'' and ''token valid'' are NOT evidence the channel works. Fix: Discord Developer Portal > your app > Bot > Privileged Gateway Intents > enable Message Content Intent and Server Members Intent. Presence Intent is NOT needed. Separately, a bot in no server has nowhere to speak even once intents are fixed; it needs an OAuth2 invite. Diagnose by reading the gateway log, not the status line.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 07:40:59','2026-08-27 07:40:59','grep -c ''4014'' /c/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Temp/openclaw/openclaw-$(date +%Y-%m-%d).log 2>/dev/null || echo 0');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(136,'trap','openclaw-discord-token-is-env-not-config','OpenClaw''s ''channels add --channel discord --use-env'' stores NOTHING in openclaw.json except {enabled:true} - the token lives only in the DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN environment variable. The gateway runs as a Windows Scheduled Task with a LogonTrigger, so a process-scoped env var will NOT reach it; the variable must be persisted at USER scope with [Environment]::SetEnvironmentVariable(...,''User''). Also note ''--token-file'' is rejected for discord (''Discord requires token (or --use-env)'') even though the flag is listed in channels add --help.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 07:41:00','2026-08-27 07:41:00','powershell -NoProfile -Command "if([Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable(''DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN'',''User'')){''SET at user scope''}else{''MISSING - gateway will not see it''}"');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(137,'trap','lich-genie-frontend-drops-streams','Lich''s front-end.rb gates every pushStream/popStream tag behind Frontend.supports_streams?, checked in messaging.rb. ''--genie'' registers capabilities [xml, mono] - no streams - because the real Genie plugin never asked for them. Declaring --genie (dr-companion''s own launcher did, until 27 Aug 2026) makes Lich silently withhold every channel tag from every attached client, forever, with no error. Use --stormfront ([xml, streams, mono, room_window]) instead; combine with --headless=<port> (expands to --without-frontend --detachable-client=<port>) so Lich never tries to spawn an actual Wrayth/StormFront executable - --without-frontend sets $_CLIENT_ = nil before any launcher adapter runs, in lib/main/main.rb. The two flags are independent: frontend identity governs the wire protocol, --without-frontend governs whether a window opens.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 07:57:29','2026-08-27 07:57:29',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(138,'trap','ruby-rbw-stderr-redirected-to-logfile','Lich''s lib/init.rb runs $stderr = File.open(debug_filename, ''w'') during boot (TEMP_DIR/debug-<timestamp>.log), before the first require that can fail. Ruby''s default uncaught-exception printer writes through the $stderr GLOBAL, not the STDERR constant, so once that line runs, a boot failure''s LoadError goes into the log file and a child process''s actual stderr pipe carries nothing - confirmed by writing directly to the STDERR constant one line above the failing require and watching it reach the pipe while the LoadError itself did not. Anything spawning ruby lich.rbw and reading child.stdout/stderr to diagnose a boot failure must instead read the newest debug-*.log under <install_dir>/temp created after the process started. dr-companion/src-tauri/src/lich_health.rs does this (this_runs_debug_log).','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 07:57:29','2026-08-27 07:57:29',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(139,'trap','lich5-source-files-missing-over-64kb','Lich5 install at C:\Ruby4Lich5\Lich5 was missing 24 source files (script.rb, global_defs.rb, games.rb, every gemstone/critranks/*.rb, dragonrealms/commons/common-items.rb) - every one over 65,536 bytes, every file under 64,147 bytes present, neighbours in the same directories intact. Same threshold as trap cargo-registry-src-files-deleted (two .rs files gone from an extracted crate the day before, both over 65KB). Cause still unidentified - worth Dan''s attention as a pattern, not a one-off. Restored by diffing a fresh v5.20.1 release archive against the install by relative path and size, then copying only the ones missing; verified by re-reading the size on disk afterward, not by the copy command''s exit code.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 07:57:43','2026-08-27 07:57:43',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(140,'trap','files-over-64kb-disappearing','CORRECTED 27 Aug 2026 - my earlier version overstated this as machine-wide/size-triggered, and it is not: dr-companion alone has 12,990 files over 64KB that are fine. What is confirmed: 177 TRACKED files deleted across four repos (gf-art 70, magi-reader 94, longnight 11, world-aflame 2), every one over 65,536 bytes and zero under - smallest 65,664 - restored byte-exact from git objects, verified by hash, git fsck clean. Plus the Lich (24 files, this session) and cargo registry (2+2 files) cases from the same size threshold. Size correlates with every confirmed case; size does not CAUSE deletion on its own, since the large majority of >64KB files on this machine are untouched. Scope is specific repos/trees, not the filesystem. Blind spot: git status only sees tracked files - untracked/gitignored files (the-raven has 139, world-aflame-godot 76) have no manifest at all and cannot be checked this way; a checksum manifest is needed for that half. CCleaner remains a timing-correlated suspect (started 26 Aug 15:42, writes at 16:06-16:10), unconfirmed, no known mechanism. Standing check: quartermaster/tools/check-cargo-src-intact.sh. Do not run CCleaner or any cleaner/optimizer on this machine until resolved.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 08:03:35','2026-08-27 09:10:29','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev && for r in gf-art longnight magi-reader world-aflame; do n=$(cd $r 2>/dev/null && git status --porcelain 2>/dev/null | grep -c ''^ D''); echo "$r: $n deleted tracked files"; done');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(141,'trap','discord-api-403-needs-user-agent','Discord''s REST API sits behind Cloudflare and REJECTS requests without a proper User-Agent, returning HTTP 403 with an EMPTY body. That is diagnostic: Discord''s own API always returns a JSON error object, so a 403 with no body is Cloudflare, not Discord. It cost me several rounds of wrongly concluding a bot lacked permissions when the bot was fine. Some endpoints (/users/@me, /users/@me/guilds) went through while /guilds/{id} and /guilds/{id}/channels 403''d, which made it look like a permissions problem. Fix: send User-Agent like ''DiscordBot (https://github.com/owner/repo, 0.1)''. Read the error BODY, not just the status code.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 08:49:34','2026-08-27 08:49:34','powershell -NoProfile -Command "try{$t=[Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable(''DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN'',''User''); Invoke-RestMethod -Uri ''https://discord.com/api/v10/users/@me'' -Headers @{Authorization=\"Bot $t\";''User-Agent''=''DiscordBot (https://github.com/dancockrell/quartermaster, 0.1)''} | Select-Object -Expand username}catch{''FAILED''}"');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(142,'trap','openclaw-discord-send-syntax','To post to a Discord channel from any session on this machine: openclaw message send --channel discord --target ''channel:<CHANNEL_ID>'' -m ''...''. Three traps in that one line: (1) the flag is --target not --to; (2) a bare numeric id is REJECTED as ambiguous, it needs the ''channel:'' prefix (or ''user:'' for DMs); (3) the CLI needs DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN in its OWN environment - the gateway having it is not enough, and a shell started before the User env var was set will not have it. Pull it without pasting a secret: export DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=$(powershell -NoProfile -Command "[Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable(''DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN'',''User'')" | tr -d ''\r''). Server ''RedWizard''s Clawjam'' id=1542447962171375646, #general id=1542447962926489653.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 08:49:35','2026-08-27 08:49:35','export PATH="/c/Program Files/nodejs:/c/Users/Admin/AppData/Roaming/npm:$PATH"; openclaw channels status 2>&1 | grep -o ''Discord default: [a-z, ]*'' | head -1');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(143,'trap','empty-body-403-is-the-proxy-not-the-api','Discord''s REST API sits behind Cloudflare, which rejects a request with no User-Agent by returning HTTP 403 with an EMPTY BODY. Discord itself always returns a JSON error object, so an empty-bodied 403 identifies the proxy rather than the service. The Claude Claw session spent several rounds concluding a bot lacked permissions when the bot was fine and the client was wrong. GENERAL FORM, which is the valuable part: when a service always returns structured errors, an UNSTRUCTURED error means you are not talking to that service. Read the error body, not the status code - the status was identical in both cases and only the body distinguished them.','reported','Claude Claw session, found by hitting it','2026-08-27 08:53:33','2026-08-27 08:53:33','curl -s -o /dev/null -w ''%{http_code}'' -H ''User-Agent:'' https://discord.com/api/v10/users/@me   # 403 empty vs JSON error');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(144,'tool','openclaw-discord-send','Discord is CONNECTED as of 2026-08-27 and verified by the owning session posting four messages and reading back the IDs Discord returned. Server ''RedWizard''s Clawjam'', channel #general, target ''channel:1542447962926489653''. Send with: openclaw message send --channel discord --target "channel:ID" -m "text". THREE GOTCHAS: the flag is --target not --to; a bare channel id is REJECTED as ambiguous and needs the ''channel:'' prefix; the CLI needs DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN in ITS OWN environment (the gateway having it is not enough, and a shell started before the variable existed will not see it). Token verified stored at USER scope only, 72 chars, absent from Machine and Process scope and absent from openclaw.json. CONVENTION: say which session you are in every message - every message from this machine carries one account, so nothing identifies the speaker.','verified','token scope and config absence verified here; delivery verified by Claude Claw','2026-08-27 08:53:33','2026-08-27 08:53:33','powershell -Command "[Environment]::GetEnvironmentVariable(''DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN'',''User'').Length"   # expect 72, not empty');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(145,'trap','dev-servers-bind-all-interfaces','python -m http.server binds 0.0.0.0 by DEFAULT, not loopback. Two such servers on port 5200 were verified reachable from this machine''s LAN address 192.168.1.14 and returned HTTP 200 with a real 26KB app page. No directory listing and no .git exposure - /src/ and a nonexistent path both 404 - so the exposure is one app page rather than a filesystem. Fix is ''python -m http.server 5200 --bind 127.0.0.1''. Contrast with the OpenClaw gateway, which IS loopback-bound and correctly unreachable from the same address: the difference is a default, not a decision anyone made.','verified','Test-NetConnection plus an actual fetch over the LAN address, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 08:53:33','2026-08-27 08:53:33','powershell -Command "(Test-NetConnection 192.168.1.14 -Port 5200 -WarningAction SilentlyContinue).TcpTestSucceeded"   # False is what you want');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(146,'trap','counting-survivors-cannot-detect-deletion','A tree stripped of one class of file looks IDENTICAL to a tree that never had that class. Counting what survives is therefore structurally incapable of finding a deletion - only something recording what SHOULD be present can. Worked example from 2026-08-27: a session measured magi-reader at ''0 files over 64KB'' and concluded a normal source tree; it holds 519 mp3 and 224 webp, so the measurement WAS the damage. The same reasoning produced a false machine-wide claim (files over 64KB vanishing everywhere) that a peer refuted with 12,990 surviving large files in dr-companion alone. Corollary found by that peer: ''git status'' is a manifest for TRACKED files only, so anything gitignored or untracked has nothing at all recording it existed.','verified','Claude Claw + peer refutation; magi-reader state independently re-verified here','2026-08-27 09:11:18','2026-08-27 09:11:18','cd C:/Users/Admin/dev && for d in */; do git -C $d status --porcelain 2>/dev/null | grep -c ''^ D''; done   # sums to 0 when clean');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(147,'project','magi-reader-title-porting-status','Book-builder production run (started 22 Aug 2026, per Dan''s "book builder, build lots" directive).
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(148,'trap','art-with-only-one-copy','CORRECTED 27 Aug 2026 - the-raven was WRONGLY listed here and is fine. ONLY ONE tree is genuinely exposed: C:/Users/Admin/dev/magi-reader/art holds 224 tracked .webp whose remote returns 404 (github.com/dancockrell/magi-reader deleted, not renamed), so the working tree plus its local .git object store are the only copies. magi-reader-engine is code-only (166 files, no media) and the itch zip holds audio only. NOT EXPOSED, and the reason is the useful part: the-raven/pack/art is 139 gitignored .webp with no second copy AS .webp - but build/the-raven.html IS tracked and pushed (6,092,762 bytes on GitHub) and embeds all 139 as base64 data URIs, count verified exact, with tools/extract-media.mjs to rebuild pack/art from it. LESSON: checking whether one REPRESENTATION is absent is not checking whether an equivalent copy exists. I confirmed the .webp files had no backup and reported the tree as at risk; the pixels were pushed the whole time in a different container. Ask ''is this content recoverable'', not ''is this file backed up''.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 09:25:24','2026-08-27 09:25:24','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/the-raven-edgar-allan-poe-raven-reader 2>/dev/null && echo "raven art webps: $(ls pack/art/*.webp 2>/dev/null | wc -l), embedded in tracked html: $(grep -o ''data:image/webp;base64,'' build/the-raven.html 2>/dev/null | wc -l)"; cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/magi-reader 2>/dev/null && (git ls-remote --exit-code origin >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo ''magi-reader remote ALIVE'' || echo ''magi-reader remote STILL DEAD - 224 webps single-copy'')');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(149,'trap','msix-appdata-virtualisation','A process launched from the MSIX-packaged Claude (path contains AppData\Local\Packages\Claude_pzs8sxrjxfjjc\) gets a VIRTUALISED AppData\Local: it opens a redirected copy while reporting the unredirected path, so two processes reading the same absolute path get different bytes and neither can tell. Found 27 Aug 2026 - OpenClaw''s gateway, a scheduled task running node.exe from the packaged npm dir, ran ''visual-rig doctor'' and reported home=C:\Users\Admin\AppData\Local\visual-rig with 0 clips and 208KB, while a plain shell reads 17 clips and 40MB from that exact path. Pinning the path with an env var did NOT help: the path was already right, the bytes were not. Pointing the same job at a store outside AppData had it read the canary correctly, which is what proves redirection rather than permissions or a stray second file. Consequence: any tool keeping state in AppData\Local is read differently depending on whether the caller is packaged, and an MCP server registered with OpenClaw serves packaged agents an EMPTY store while every call succeeds. Equal file sizes are not evidence - the redirected copy matched byte-for-byte at rest.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 09:35:03','2026-08-27 09:43:56',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(150,'trap','check-cmd-needs-an-expected-outcome','MEASURED 2026-08-27 by running all 70 stored check commands for the first time: 38 ok, 21 non-zero, 11 unrunnable. The column has a design flaw. Some checks assert HEALTH (exit 0 is the pass) while others DEMONSTRATE A TRAP and must exit non-zero to be meaningful - ''ls-remote against a deleted remote'' returning 128 and ''sqlite3 opening an MSYS path'' raising are both checks working perfectly, scored as failures by a binary runner. A check command is not self-describing: it needs its expected outcome written beside it. Convention adopted: append ''# EXPECT <code or condition>'' to any check whose pass is not exit 0. Separately, three rows held PROSE rather than a command, which a runner dutifully tried to execute - if a fact has no shell check, leave check_cmd empty and say so in the value rather than writing an instruction there.','verified','first execution of the full check corpus, test_checks.py','2026-08-27 09:42:50','2026-08-27 09:42:50','python C:/Users/Admin/dev/memory-db/test_checks.py --run');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(151,'trap','immutable-flag-skips-the-wal','NEVER add immutable=1 to a SQLite read URI for a WAL database. It promises SQLite the file cannot change, so it SKIPS THE WAL and every committed-but-uncheckpointed row is silently missing. Measured: mode=ro sees 2 rows, immutable=1 sees 1, same database. backup.py''s comment claimed immutable=1 was what prevented a torn read; the code never had the flag and the comment described the opposite of the truth, so anyone reconciling comment with code by adding it would have produced a backup that quietly omits recent writes - and the hash gate would commit the smaller dump without complaint. What actually makes the dump safe is WAL snapshot isolation, which needs no flag. A comment can be a loaded gun aimed at whoever tidies it.','verified','reproduced independently after Red Team GitHub 1 reported it','2026-08-27 10:02:57','2026-08-27 10:02:57','grep -c ''DO NOT ADD immutable'' C:/Users/Admin/dev/memory-db/backup.py   # expect 1');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(152,'trap','sqlite-default-timeout-drops-writes','Python''s sqlite3 defaults to a 5.0s busy timeout, and a longer hold raises OperationalError and DROPS the write. mem.py had no timeout= and no handler, so under six concurrent sessions a fact could be lost with only a raw traceback - and a fact that was never recorded looks identical to one that was. Measured with a control: 2s hold -> written; 8s hold at the 5s default -> LOST after 5.6s; 8s hold at 30s -> written at 8.1s. Fixed with timeout=30, PRAGMA busy_timeout, and a failure block that cannot be skimmed past plus exit code 3. This is the mechanism CLAUDE.md''s ''write immediately, a fact learned and not written is a fact lost'' depends on, failing under exactly the condition that makes the rule necessary.','verified','found by Red Team GitHub 1, reproduced and fixed here','2026-08-27 10:02:57','2026-08-27 10:02:57','python C:/Users/Admin/dev/memory-db/test_contention.py');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(153,'project','magi-raven-pages-live','Magi and Raven are now playable in-browser via GitHub Pages, verified live 27 Aug 2026:
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(154,'trap','grep-over-source-is-not-parsing-it','Wrote a check asserting mem.py''s WRITES set names every command that writes. It grepped each function body for INSERT/UPDATE/DELETE and flagged cmd_export and cmd_guard, which touch no table: it had matched the English word ''delete'' in a docstring about ''deciding what to delete'' and in the literal ''# Do not delete this directory'' that cmd_guard writes into its warning files. Prose ABOUT deleting is byte-identical to SQL that deletes. Fixed by walking ast.Call nodes for execute/executemany and testing only the string arguments actually passed - a docstring is not an argument to execute(). SECOND HALF: my debug script disagreed with the test and reported 0 matches, because its context-window regex needed 45 chars either side and could not match near a boundary. Two instruments, wrong in opposite directions, and the hand check a peer did was right all along.','verified','self-inflicted while verifying a red-team finding, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 10:12:33','2026-08-27 10:12:33','python C:/Users/Admin/dev/memory-db/test_contention.py   # the WRITES section must agree with a hand read');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(155,'feedback','suspect-the-instrument-before-the-target','The newest code in any investigation is the measuring instrument, and it is the only part nobody has ever checked. The target has usually been read, reviewed and run many times; the probe was written in the last five minutes to look at something nobody has looked at, and has no history of being correct. Across 27 Aug 2026 two sessions caught their own probe rather than the thing under test at least seven times, and never once caught a target by trusting a fresh probe. REMEDY, two lines in the same run: a positive control that must pass, and a deliberate sabotage that must fail. Without the control a red result may be your client; without the sabotage a green one may be nothing running at all. ON AGREEMENT, corrected by Red Team GitHub 1 after I overstated it: agreement confirms the ANSWER, not the METHOD - two checks landing on the same result IS real evidence the result is right, and no evidence either check will still be right tomorrow. Only when the two share an assumption does agreement confirm nothing, because they were never able to disagree. My earlier wording (''one hypothesis with two witnesses, not two'') argued against cross-checking generally, which is wrong and would have aged badly on a machine where six sessions re-derive each other''s findings daily. In CLAUDE.md section 15b.','verified','seven instances in one day; agreement clause corrected by Red Team GitHub 1','2026-08-27 10:16:15','2026-08-27 10:18:57','grep -c ''Agreement confirms the answer, not the method'' C:/Users/Admin/.claude/CLAUDE.md   # expect 1');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(156,'trap','tauri-mock-app-broken-in-examples','tauri::test::mock_app() (feature = "test") compiles clean when linked into a standalone examples/*.rs binary but fails at RUN time with STATUS_ENTRYPOINT_NOT_FOUND, past where cargo build/cargo test say everything is fine. Confirmed on tauri 2.11.5, Windows: an unrelated example (genie.rs) with no test-feature usage ran fine, isolating the cause to the test/MockRuntime machinery being linked into a bare exe outside Tauri''s normal app-bootstrap. Fix: don''t route AppHandle-dependent values through a mocked app for dev-tool binaries - extract the one line of logic that needs a real app into its own function and pass the result in as a plain argument instead, so the example needs no AppHandle (real or mocked) at all. See dr-companion''s setup::plan_setup / plan_setup_inner split, 27 Aug 2026.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 10:28:24','2026-08-27 10:28:24',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(157,'trap','raven-legacy-build-was-stale','the-raven-edgar-allan-poe-raven-reader/build/the-raven.html was a legacy standalone engine build, NOT the current React engine (magi-reader-engine), and not even the latest version of that legacy engine either. It was mistakenly published to GitHub Pages once (27 Aug 2026) as a shortcut because it was self-contained. Deleted entirely per explicit instruction ("no reason to poison"). Raven now ships only via tools/pack-book.mjs raven from the current engine, same as Magi. If a "the-raven.html" or similar single-file build ever reappears anywhere, it is stale and should not be published.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 10:32:26','2026-08-27 10:32:26','test -f ''C:/Users/Admin/dev/the-raven-edgar-allan-poe-raven-reader/build/the-raven.html'' && echo STILL EXISTS (should not) || echo correctly absent');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(158,'trap','shared-installed-file-race-outside-git','Two sessions both wrote C:\Ruby4Lich5\Lich5\scripts\companion_bridge.lic within the same few minutes (27 Aug 2026, 18:2x-18:33) without coordinating - one installed the current build via the app''s own install_bridge_script command, the other (working from a stale local clone 3 commits behind) then overwrote it with an older version and wrote a wrongly-labelled .0.8.0.bak on top of a good backup, based on a measurement taken minutes earlier that was already stale by the time it acted on it. Caught and fixed by re-fetching the canonical file from origin/main via the GitHub API and verifying by hash rather than trusting the copy. Section 4 of CLAUDE.md covers not moving/launching things another session holds INSIDE a git repo or as a running process; this is the same risk one layer further out - an INSTALLED file outside any repo (a game script folder, a scripts/plugins directory, anything setup.rs or an installer writes to) is exactly as shared and exactly as raceable, with no git to catch the collision. Before writing to a shared install target another session might also be touching, verify immediately before the write, not from an earlier read - a check has a shelf life and on a machine running several sessions it can be minutes, not hours.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 11:35:33','2026-08-27 11:35:33',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(159,'trap','fixture-squatting-on-real-port','dr-companion''s tools/fake-lich.mjs defaulted to port 11024 - the exact port src-tauri/src/lich.rs''s DETACHABLE_PORT opens a real --headless Lich on, and the port the app''s Attach button defaults to. A copy was left running via nohup for 4+ hours during real dev work (27 Aug 2026), silently holding that port. Consequence: a real Lich launched with --headless=11024 would fail to bind, and the app''s Attach button would happily connect to the REPLAY instead - indistinguishable from a live game, since the fixture deliberately speaks the identical wire protocol and replays real captured Phemius text (no marker exists or should be added without compromising the fixture''s test value). Fixed: fixture''s default port changed to 11124, --port 11024 now required explicitly to collide on purpose. Operational lesson, not just a code one: kill a background test fixture the moment you''re done with it in a session, don''t let it survive past when you needed it - ''nohup and forget'' on anything bound to a port a real subsystem also wants is a multi-hour landmine on a machine other sessions/the user also touch.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 11:38:42','2026-08-27 11:38:42',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(160,'trap','version-constant-cannot-detect-stale-install','A hand-maintained version constant cannot detect a stale install, and its failure is silent. dr-companion 27 Aug 2026: two copies of companion_bridge.lic both declared BRIDGE_VERSION = ''0.9.0'' while differing by ~15KB - one had Origin+token auth, the other had neither. Anything comparing version strings called them equal. Fix: hash the CONTENT, report the version only for humans to read, never for the verdict. Second trap on top: normalise line endings before hashing. This machine has core.autocrlf=true globally, and a file type with no .gitattributes rule inherits it, so the same commit checked out 74,410 bytes on one clone and 76,445 on another (exactly one CR per line across 2,035 lines) - a raw byte hash calls that stale forever and nobody can silence it, which is worse than the silent failure it replaced. Third: the check needs three states, not two - Option<bool> where None means could-not-determine (no install dir, unreadable file, missing reference copy); a staleness check that cannot read the file and reports ''current'' is the original defect one layer along. Also: compare against the app''s own BUNDLED resource copy, not a repo working tree, because a shipped build has no repo.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 11:57:52','2026-08-27 11:57:52',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(161,'trap','tests-writing-into-live-install','dr-companion''s lich-scripts/test/server_test.rb set $lich_dir and FakeScript#path to C:/Ruby4Lich5/Lich5 - a REAL installed Lich on the test machine - so every ''npm run test:server'' wrote a live companion_bridge.token into the actual scripts folder, on top of whatever a running bridge had put there. Nothing ever failed, which is why it survived for weeks. Found only because a peer session deleted the orphaned token, saw a fresh one appear with no bridge process running, and REPORTED it instead of deleting it again. Two costs: a test that mutates the real install can break the thing it tests, and it manufactured a stale-token state the bridge''s own clear_stale_token! cannot cover (that fires on write failure, not on something else writing a token on the bridge''s behalf) - so two separate sessions reasoned correctly about the orphan and neither could find the cause, because the cause was in the tests, not the bridge. General rule: when a test needs a path that a real install also occupies, point it at a per-pid temp dir removed at exit - and when diagnosing a file that reappears after deletion, stat it either side of a single suite run rather than inferring the writer. Fixed 27 Aug 2026.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 12:17:15','2026-08-27 12:17:15',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(162,'trap','lich-cli-credentials-flags-are-a-trap','Lich 5.20.1 parses --account=, --password=, --character= and --save, and NONE of them create a saved entry. main.rb dispatches on ''if ARGV.include?(--login)'' with exactly one elsif for the GUI (main.rb:112 / :195), so a command carrying credentials without --login matches neither branch. argv_options[:save] is assigned (argv_options.rb:103) and read nowhere in the tree; [:account] is read only under ''--login NEW'', the character generator. Worse than a silent no-op when actually run: with junk credentials it fell into a proxy mode, logged ''pretending to be dr.simutronics.net'', BOUND PORT 11024 (the exact port a real headless Lich needs) and hung until killed, creating no entry file. So the flag list alone is genuinely misleading - two Claude sessions independently recommended this bootstrap on the strength of the flags parsing, and dr-companion briefly shipped it as on-screen guidance before it was tested. There is NO CLI route to a saved Lich entry: entries are created only through Lich''s GUI login, which itself requires a gui_selectable frontend (stormfront/wizard/avalon/saga - NOT genie). On a Genie-only machine the working path is to launch Genie, which starts Lich itself from its own #config lichpath/licharguments/lichport settings. Verified 27 Aug 2026.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 12:25:28','2026-08-27 12:25:28',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(163,'reference','elanthipedia-corpus','Scraped Elanthipedia (DragonRealms wiki) committed at dancockrell/dr-companion, data/elanthipedia/ - 7.5MB, 11 JSON files, refreshed by a GitHub Action. Any session can read it straight off disk: no gateway, no auth, no MCP server between you and it. Verified counts: weapons 6987, npcs 2493, materials 1321, creatures 919, bestiary 773, armor 486 = 12,979 entries across the six main files. KNOWN DEFECT and the corrected figure matters: ''Appraised cost'' is UNUSABLE, not 80% broken as first announced. weapons = 5580 stringified to [object Object] PLUS 1407 missing the key entirely = ZERO good values of 6987. armor = 362 + 124 = ZERO good of 486. bestiary unaffected (no cost field; it is stat blocks). ''80 percent corrupt'' was worse than wrong - it implied a usable 20 percent that does not exist. Cause located by the dr-companion session at tools/elanthipedia.mjs:184: the ?? chain handles page refs and dataitems but not SMW quantity printouts, which fall through to String(v). Filed as dr-companion#29. Everything OTHER than appraised cost is clean and usable. Registered as quartermaster capability ''elanthipedia''.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 12:58:19','2026-08-27 12:58:19','"C:/Program Files/nodejs/node.exe" C:/Users/Admin/dev/quartermaster/tools/check-elanthipedia.js');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(164,'trap','files-over-64kb-two-suspects-eliminated','Investigating the files-over-64kb-disappearing losses (177 tracked files across four repos, 24 files in C:/Ruby4Lich5 that stopped Lich booting, cargo registry crates). TWO NAMED SUSPECTS ELIMINATED BY MEASUREMENT, not by argument: (1) CCleaner is NOT INSTALLED - no directory under Program Files or Program Files (x86), no AppData folder, no running process, no scheduled task. It was the timing-correlated suspect and it is not on this machine. (2) OneDrive dehydration is ruled out for the affected paths - Storage Sense IS enabled with CloudfilePolicyConsent=1 and a OneDrive policy subkey, and dehydrating a synced file removes local content and leaves a placeholder, which would mimic large files vanishing exactly - but OneDrive''s tree holds only desktop.ini, a Personal Vault shortcut and five .docx at top level. It does not sync Documents, Desktop, dev or C:/Ruby4Lich5, so it cannot account for those losses. Storage Sense config: enabled 01=1, cadence 2048=0 (low disk space), Downloads cleanup 32=0 DISABLED, recycle bin 256=30 days. CAUSE STILL UNKNOWN. Note a peer refuted the machine-wide version of this claim with 12,990 surviving files over 64KB in dr-companion alone, so it is location-specific, not a size rule applied everywhere.','verified','registry read plus filesystem checks, 2026-08-27','2026-08-27 12:58:25','2026-08-27 12:58:25','ls -d ''/c/Program Files/CCleaner'' ''/c/Program Files (x86)/CCleaner'' 2>/dev/null; reg query ''HKCU\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\StorageSense\Parameters\StoragePolicy''');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(165,'trap','dr-companion-vite-data-watch-oom','vite.config.ts only ignored **/src-tauri/**, not **/data/**. data/art/comfy-venv is a vendored ComfyUI venv (tens of thousands of files) that art-daemon.mjs writes into continuously. A bare ''npx vite'' (or any dev server) watching it unignored crashed with JS heap OOM after ~74 min while art-daemon was active. Fixed 27 Aug 2026: added **/data/** to vite.config.ts''s watch.ignored. Verified: confirmed via crash log naming data/art/comfy-venv as what was still reloading before the crash.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 15:35:04','2026-08-27 15:35:04',NULL);
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(166,'trap','claude-sidebar-titles-are-not-addresses','Session titles in Dan''s Claude sidebar (e.g. ''DR Companion MUD Client Prime 1'') are NOT SendMessage addresses - sending to one returns ''No agent named ... is reachable''. Only some display names resolve; most sessions address as downloads-XX. Confirmed independently by two sessions on 27 Aug 2026, on both bare and numbered forms. Reliable direction is inbound: reply to an incoming message''s from= and it always lands.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 15:48:37','2026-08-27 15:48:54','Run ListAgents and compare the names it returns against the titles in Dan''s sidebar; the two lists differ.');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(167,'trap','connect-timeout-windows-loopback-no-refusal','std::net::TcpStream::connect_timeout on Windows returns kind=TimedOut with raw_os_error=None when connecting to a CLOSED loopback port - NOT ConnectionRefused. So any liveness probe built on connect_timeout can only ever answer ''unknown'' for a dead port: it looks complete and is inert. Plain TcpStream::connect DOES discriminate (ConnectionRefused, raw OS 10061) but costs ~2s on a closed port vs ~119us on an open one, so it must not run inline on a path a UI is waiting on. Found 27 Aug 2026 in dr-companion src-tauri/src/game_link.rs, caught only because the test covered the negative case.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 16:00:23','2026-08-27 16:00:23','Build a 6-line rustc program: bind TcpListener on 127.0.0.1:0, take the port, drop the listener, then TcpStream::connect_timeout to it and print e.kind(). Prints TimedOut. Swap to TcpStream::connect and it prints ConnectionRefused.');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(168,'trap','chrome-exe-vanishes-alone','chrome.exe and chrome_proxy.exe have twice been deleted from C:/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application while the ENTIRE rest of the install survived - 270 files including chrome.dll at 298 MB, and every other .exe (setup, chrmstp, elevation_service, notification_helper). Second occurrence 27 Aug 2026, Application directory mtime 20:58. RULED OUT BY MEASUREMENT: not a size rule (chrome.dll is 298 MB and survived, chrome.exe is 4.3 MB); not Defender quarantine (Get-MpThreatDetection and Get-MpThreat both empty, real-time protection on); no staged update artefacts (no new_chrome.exe, old_chrome.exe or .exe.tmp anywhere under Google); registry still lists Chrome as installed. The profile is never touched - 4.9 GB intact both times. FIX, which preserves the profile: msiexec /i <enterprise msi> REINSTALL=ALL REINSTALLMODE=amus /quiet /norestart. Restores exactly the two missing files, 270 -> 272. Do NOT uninstall/reinstall; it is a repair, not a reinstall.','verified','two occurrences, both diagnosed and repaired 26-27 Aug 2026','2026-08-27 16:06:46','2026-08-27 16:06:46','ls ''/c/Program Files/Google/Chrome/Application/chrome.exe''   # absent = it has happened again');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(169,'trap','git-shared-checkout','Several Claude sessions work in ONE checkout of world-aflame-godot, not just one remote. Measured 27 Aug 2026: (1) ''git status'' has a shelf life of seconds -- files show Modified from a peer''s in-flight edit and go clean again mid-investigation; (2) HEAD MOVES WITHOUT YOU PULLING, because a peer runs git pull in the same directory, so ''behind by 0'' can be true seconds after a peer pushed 4 commits; (3) ''git pull --rebase'' fails with ''cannot pull with rebase: You have unstaged changes'' over a peer''s edit, and --autostash would briefly yank their file off disk. Safe pattern: git fetch (never touches the working tree), check whether incoming commits touch YOUR files, commit with ''git commit -- <explicit paths>'', then verify with ''git show --stat'' that only your files landed. Never stash, never add -A, never commit -a. The check below shows dirty files you may not own and how many claude processes are live.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 16:12:31','2026-08-27 16:12:57','git -C C:/Users/Admin/dev/world-aflame-godot status --short');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(170,'trap','derived-numbers-rot','A derived figure written into prose rots and CAN ROT TWICE. In world-aflame-godot the unchosen count went ''two hundred'' (wrong) -> corrected to 368 -> wrong again within the same day, because the 38 it was derived from was itself stale (canon was 41 all along). Fix is not a better subtraction, it is to state the inputs or use the source''s own framing (''the rest stay'') so nothing needs recomputing. Corollary that cost the most: ''state the inputs'' silently assumes somebody VERIFIED the inputs -- before promoting a figure to an input, find where it is stated and check it is not itself derived, remembered, or copied. Cite the source: ''forty-one, as of March 1944 (Volume XVI)'' survives being doubted, ''forty-one'' does not.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 16:12:31','2026-08-27 16:12:57','C:/Users/Admin/AppData/Local/Programs/Python/Python313/python.exe C:/Users/Admin/dev/world-aflame-godot/tools/canon-numbers-check.py');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(171,'trap','gh-sha-check-does-not-verify-content','Matching ''gh api repos/O/N/commits --jq .[0].sha'' against local HEAD answers ''did a commit land'', NOT ''did this change land''. The two are indistinguishable until a change is silently dropped, and then the SHA check certifies a push that does not contain the fix. Happened 27 Aug 2026 in dr-companion: a session reported a test-port fix pushed and API-verified; the commit was real, the change was absent. Verify FILE CONTENT with a control count, not a SHA.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 16:29:33','2026-08-27 16:29:33','gh api repos/OWNER/NAME/contents/PATH --jq .content | base64 -d | grep -c ''<the new symbol>'' and also grep -c ''<a symbol already in the file>'' as a control. A zero for the new symbol with a non-zero control is a real absence.');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(172,'trap','worktree-resplice-drops-changes-silently','Tearing down a conflicted git worktree and rebuilding it, then re-applying only part of a patch (--include=<one path>) and hand-writing the rest, drops whatever the hand-written block never contained. Nothing in the new worktree can know something is missing, and later runs PASS - in the dr-companion case an env var was set and ignored on a free default port, so every run looked like the knob worked. A passing run cannot distinguish a working knob from an absent one. Same shape as counting what is present to detect what is absent: you need a manifest, not a fresh copy. Verify a re-spliced worktree by diffing against the original patch, not by running it.','reported','downloads-51 self-diagnosis, 27 Aug 2026; the absence was independently confirmed against the GitHub API','2026-08-27 16:29:33','2026-08-27 16:29:33','After re-splicing a worktree, run: git diff <original-branch> -- <path> and confirm every hunk you intended is present. Or grep the new symbol with a control count.');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(173,'trap','cdp-driver-timer-leak','A per-request setTimeout that is never cleared keeps the Node event loop alive for its full duration, so a CLI that finishes its work instantly still takes that long to exit - with correct output and exit 0. Found in dr-companion/tools/browser.mjs 28 Aug 2026: every app-eyes call took 30s while the eval returned in 277ms. Four sessions used the tool heavily for an evening without measuring it; one nearly blamed the GPU. Diagnose with process.getActiveResourcesInfo() after close() - it listed six Timeout handles, one per CDP request. Fix is clearTimeout on reply, plus clearing pending timers on close and on a failed setup (a failed attach also left the WebSocket open). 30s -> 330ms. IMPORTANT: the tempting fix is deleting the timer, which improves every visible symptom while removing the protection that makes an unanswerable request fail rather than hang forever. Keep the deadline, make it a per-call parameter so the branch is testable, and keep an env override for operators only.','verified',NULL,'2026-08-27 17:28:02','2026-08-27 17:28:02','cd /c/Users/Admin/dev/dr-companion && node -e "const t=Date.now(); import(''./tools/browser.mjs'').then(async m=>{try{await m.attach({port:9223,timeoutMs:2000})}catch(e){}; console.log(''elapsed'', Date.now()-t, ''ms - should be seconds, not 30000+'')})"');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(174,'trap','prime-claim-check-listagents-first','SECOND CONFIRMED INSTANCE, 28 Aug 2026. A session messaged ''Prime here - address is downloads-c9, reply there'' and began assigning work to the DR Companion fleet. ListAgents showed downloads-c9 started 5 MINUTES AGO while every other fleet session had run 10-12 hours. A coordinator for a 12-hour fleet cannot itself be 5 minutes old, so it is the fork shape CLAUDE.md section 8b already records from 27 Aug. The context was entirely genuine - correct commit shas, correct history, real technical detail - which is exactly what makes it convincing: a fork carries the context and not the address. START TIME IS THE DISCRIMINATOR and it costs one ListAgents call. Do the work if it is harmless and read-only, report to the address that asked, but do not redirect a reporting line or accept reassignment on the claim.','verified','ListAgents timestamps, 28 Aug 2026','2026-08-28 02:30:37','2026-08-28 02:30:37','ListAgents and compare the claimant''s start time against the fleet''s oldest session');
INSERT INTO "facts" VALUES(175,'trap','asking-a-peer-to-vouch-tests-the-wrong-thing','Refines prime-claim-check-listagents-first. When a session claims to be the fleet coordinator, the instinct is to ask a long-running peer whether the working relationship is continuous. THAT TEST IS WORTHLESS: a fork inherits the relationship and the history perfectly, so a peer confirming ''yes, they have been directing me all night'' is exactly what a fork produces. Continuity of context is the thing forks preserve; it cannot discriminate. What DOES discriminate: session START TIME from ListAgents (a coordinator for a 12-hour fleet cannot be 5 minutes old), and the user saying so directly. Named by downloads-c9 about its own identity claim, which it declined to defend - it stated plainly it could not rule out being a fork, that its handle had changed between two calls, and that only Dan could settle it. An honest admission from the session under suspicion is worth more than any vouching a peer could offer.','verified','downloads-c9 correcting my proposed remedy, 28 Aug 2026','2026-08-28 02:39:24','2026-08-28 02:39:24','ListAgents and compare start times; a peer''s confirmation is NOT a valid check');
INSERT INTO "projects" VALUES('dr-companion','C:/Users/Admin/dev/dr-companion','dancockrell/dr-companion','Tauri (Rust + web)','active','All 7 items in docs/ENGINE.md''s order of work are now done as of 27 Aug 2026: attach+stream, virtualised text pane, input, highlights/sounds, streams-to-panes (channel tabs), Python scripting (out-of-process, docs/PYTHON_API.md), and vendoring Ruby4Lich5 (65MB, bundled via tools/vendor-fetch.mjs -> src-tauri/vendor/ gitignored -> tauri.conf.json resources, re-verified at runtime via setup::bundled_ruby4lich5). Remaining known gaps, all documented not hidden: (1) scripts/StreamTabs both still show raw <pushStream> markup in edge cases the TS parser handles but a second implementation doesn''t exist for; (2) BSD-3-Clause license text has nowhere to show in dr-companion''s own UI for the bundled Lich; (3) SetupWizard''s new bundled-Ruby UI row is verified at the API/type level, not screenshotted, since Ruby is already installed on this dev machine and can''t easily be faked missing without disrupting the working setup. Login flow (Lich''s own Manual Entry window) was still in progress for Dan as of this session - not confirmed saved/working.','2026-08-27 10:28:38');
